text:
GEN 1:14
Thadou: Chuin Pathen'in aseiye, “Sun le jan sepkhen dingin vanthomjol avah thei vahho hung kigol uhenlang, hiche ho chu kum kihei chin melchihnan jong, nikho simtoh nan jong chule kum simtoh nan jong pang'u hen.
English: God said, “Let there be lights in the expanse of the sky to divide the day from the night; and let them be for signs to mark seasons, days, and years;

GEN 2:11
Thadou: Vadung khatna chu ahile Pishon ahin, hiche chu sana kimuna vadung ahin Havilah gam pumpia long kimvel ahi.
English: The name of the first is Pishon: it flows through the whole land of Havilah, where there is gold;

GEN 2:16
Thadou: Ahin Pathen in mipa koma athupeh chu, “Nang man hiche honsunga theiga ho khu nadei dei naneh thei cheh ahi.
English: The LORD God commanded the man, saying, “You may freely eat of every tree of the garden;

GEN 11:10
Thadou: Hiche hi Shem insung mite thusim ahi e. Twisang let kum ni jouvin Shem chu atahsa kum jakhat alhing in achapa Arpachshad chu ahing'e;
English: This is the history of the generations of Shem: Shem was one hundred years old when he became the father of Arpachshad two years after the flood.

GEN 14:23
Thadou: Keiman patse jang khat cha hihen lang, kengchot khao jeng cha hijong leh nang thil kiti poupou khatcha kalah louhel ding ahi, nangman Abrham ka hao doh sah tai,” tia nasei thei louna ding in;
English: that I will not take a thread nor a sandal strap nor anything that is yours, lest you should say, ‘I have made Abram rich.’

GEN 15:14
Thadou: Ahin keiman hiche nam sugenthei ho chu ka phulah ding ahi, chule phat ahung sot a achaina teng amaho chu hatah a nei le gou ahin nei diu ahi.
English: I will also judge that nation, whom they will serve. Afterward they will come out with great wealth;

GEN 25:2
Thadou: Amanu chun cha hicheng hi ahing in, amaho se chu Zimran ahin, Jokshan ahin, Medan ahin, Ishbak ahin, chule Shuak ahiuvin;
English: She bore him Zimran, Jokshan, Medan, Midian, Ishbak, and Shuah.

GEN 25:7
Thadou: Abraham chu kum jakhat le kum som sagi le kum nga alhing in;
English: These are the days of the years of Abraham’s life which he lived: one hundred seventy-five years.

GEN 27:5
Thadou: Ahin Isaac le Esau kihou na chu Rebekah'in guhthim chan ana ngai jin hichun Esau chu gamleng ding a akon doh phat in;
English: Rebekah heard when Isaac spoke to Esau his son. Esau went to the field to hunt for venison, and to bring it.

GEN 28:1
Thadou: Hichun Isaac in Jacob akouvin, phatthei aboh-in chule athu lhah in ajah a hitin aseiye, “Nangman hiche Canaan numei hohi jia nakipui thei louhel ding ahi;
English: Isaac called Jacob, blessed him, and commanded him, “You shall not take a wife of the daughters of Canaan.

GEN 30:41
Thadou: Hiti chun kelngoi lah a asapha ho chu aki jang mat teng ule thingbah ho amu uva, aki jang mat theina ding uvin Jacob in jong thingbah ho amasang uva twi lonna kom laiya aga jam peh jin ahi.
English: Whenever the stronger of the flock conceived, Jacob laid the rods in front of the eyes of the flock in the watering troughs, that they might conceive among the rods;

GEN 31:17
Thadou: Hichun Jacob akipat doh in ajite le achate jouse chu Sangan chunga atoudoh sah soh kei tan;
English: Then Jacob rose up, and set his sons and his wives on the camels,

GEN 31:22
Thadou: Ahin ni thum jouvin Jacob ajam mang tai tithu chu Laban ahin seipeh un;
English: Laban was told on the third day that Jacob had fled.

GEN 31:27
Thadou: Ibola guhthim cha a najam mang uham? Ibol'a neijou lhep ham ati, chule nache ding iti dan a neihet sah lou beh ham? Neina hetsah le chun thupitah a kilhahna ankong le la a ngei tah tah kisan tin, tumging to kithoa kivai lhah ta dinga ati.
English: Why did you flee secretly, and deceive me, and didn’t tell me, that I might have sent you away with mirth and with songs, with tambourine and with harp;

GEN 36:2
Thadou: Esau in Canaan nungah ni aji din ana ki pui'in khat nu chu Hite mi Adah Elton ahi, anina nu chu ahile Oholibamah Anah chanu ahin Zibeon Hivi tedinga atunu u ahi.
English: Esau took his wives from the daughters of Canaan: Adah the daughter of Elon, the Hittite; and Oholibamah the daughter of Anah, the daughter of Zibeon, the Hivite;

GEN 37:23
Thadou: Hichun Joseph ahung lhun chun asopite hon a sangkhol chol hoitah chu asut lhah peh pai tauvin ahi.
English: When Joseph came to his brothers, they stripped Joseph of his tunic, the tunic of many colors that was on him;

GEN 40:21
Thadou: Ju vaihom pachu aju vaihom na ma man apansah kit'in, aman jong jukhon chu Pharaoh khut a agapetai.
English: He restored the chief cup bearer to his position again, and he gave the cup into Pharaoh’s hand;

GEN 41:17
Thadou: Chuin Pharaoh mang chu Joseph koma aseitai, aman hitin aseiye, “Ka mang in Nile vadung panga kana ding in.
English: Pharaoh spoke to Joseph, “In my dream, behold, I stood on the brink of the river;

GEN 41:18
Thadou: Hiche a che a chun bongchal sagi hoitah kivah thao cheh vadunga kon chun ahung doh in chule hilaiya hampa dong ho chu ane pantan ahi.
English: and behold, seven fat and sleek cattle came up out of the river. They fed in the marsh grass;

GEN 41:20
Thadou: Hiche bong agong melse tah hochun bongchal sagi athao ho chu aval lhum tan ahi.
English: The thin and ugly cattle ate up the first seven fat cattle;

GEN 41:22
Thadou: Hichun keima ka imu lhu kit'in, chule keiman mang khat kaneibe kit'in, hichea kamang achun changvui sagi vetnom umtah phungkhat a ga ka mun ahi.
English: I saw in my dream, and behold, seven heads of grain came up on one stalk, full and good;

GEN 43:4
Thadou: Benjamin keiho toh na sol khom le kache dingu anchang kaga choh dingu ahi ati.
English: If you’ll send our brother with us, we’ll go down and buy you food;

GEN 43:9
Thadou: Chule keima ka tahsa tah in mopo nang kate ijem tia boina aum khah le, ahin Benjamin chu kahin nung pui loule boina jouse keiman mo ka poh ding ahi ati; chule nangma angsunga mopoh na thepmo na jouse keima chunga chu jeng hen ati.
English: I’ll be collateral for him. From my hand will you require him. If I don’t bring him to you, and set him before you, then let me bear the blame forever;

GEN 43:11
Thadou: Chuphat in apao Israel chun ajah uva, ‘chuti ding mong ahiya ahile hiti hin ki gong uvin, gamsunga thingga phalai cheh lheng khom uvin lang, thingnai, lou them khat le khoiju them khat toh, thil namtwi toh, thei chang toh, chule jonmot chang toh nadip sunguva mipa peh ding chun posuh uvin ati.’
English: Their father, Israel, said to them, “If it must be so, then do this: Take from the choice fruits of the land in your bags, and carry down a present for the man, a little balm, a little honey, spices and myrrh, nuts, and almonds;

GEN 43:25
Thadou: Hichun amahon Joseph peh dinga ahin thilpoh houchu akigon tup uvin, chule amahon aja tauvin sunteng le Joseph toh an aneh khom ding'u thu chu;
English: They prepared the present for Joseph’s coming at noon, for they heard that they should eat bread there.

GEN 44:18
Thadou: Hichun Judah aphei chen aseitai, “Lungset tah in ka pakai koma nasoh pan thu chang khat tou kasei thei ding ham? lungset tah in nei lunghan khum hih in, nangma Pharaoh toh nalal na lhon jong ki bang ahitan;
English: Then Judah came near to him, and said, “Oh, my lord, please let your servant speak a word in my lord’s ears, and don’t let your anger burn against your servant; for you are even as Pharaoh.

GEN 44:21
Thadou: Nangman thu neina peh jal a amapa chu hinpui un keiman kamit taha kamu nom e natin;
English: You said to your servants, ‘Bring him down to me, that I may set my eyes on him.’

GEN 44:30
Thadou: Tun ka pakai keima kapa henga hiche chapang jao lou vin ki nungle thei pong kate ati, ajeh chu kapa'u hinkho le hiche chapang pa hinkho hi aman khom lhon ahiye.
English: Now therefore when I come to your servant my father, and the boy is not with us; since his life is bound up in the boy’s life;

GEN 47:29
Thadou: Israel chu athi tei ding nikho ahung nai tul tul phat in aman jong achapa Joseph akouvin ajah a “Na mit mua nangma ka lung lhaisah jouva ahile gunchu tah le kitah tah a nei bolna ding in kataipi gui noi tuhin lang Egypt gam'a neihin vuilou hel na dingin kitep in;
English: The time came near that Israel must die, and he called his son Joseph, and said to him, “If now I have found favor in your sight, please put your hand under my thigh, and deal kindly and truly with me. Please don’t bury me in Egypt,

GEN 48:15
Thadou: Hichun Jacob in Joseph phatthei aboh in hitin aseiye, “Ka Pathen kapu Abraham kapa Isaac masanga lamkai jingpa ka Pakai kelngoi chinga hung pang jing ka hinkho pumpi tuni geiya eipui hoipa;
English: He blessed Joseph, and said, “The God before whom my fathers Abraham and Isaac walked, the God who has fed me all my life long to this day,

EXO 9:15
Thadou: “Tu jeng ajong keiman ka khut ka lhan jah'a nangma le namite chung'a gamna huise ka lansah'a leiset chung'a hi kasuh mang hel jeng thei na hiye.”
English: For now I would have stretched out my hand, and struck you and your people with pestilence, and you would have been cut off from the earth;

EXO 10:1
Thadou: Chuin Pakaiyin Mose heng'a asei jin, “Pharaoh heng'a che kit inlang, ga seikit tan. Keiman ama leh a sohte ho lungthim ka suhtah ahin, melchihna hicheng jouse hi ka kilah sah ding ahi,” ati.
English: The LORD said to Moses, “Go in to Pharaoh, for I have hardened his heart and the heart of his servants, that I may show these my signs among them;

EXO 12:3
Thadou: “Israelte kikhop khomna munpi jouse ah ga seipeh lhon tan. Hiche lhasung nisom alhin niteng leh ama ama cheh in apu apateu insung kai lhah apat, insung khat cheh akon kelngoi khat cheh kat doh ding'a ahin kai diu ahiye.”
English: Speak to all the congregation of Israel, saying, ‘On the tenth day of this month, they shall take to them every man a lamb, according to their fathers’ houses, a lamb for a household;

EXO 13:17
Thadou: Ajonan Pharaoh vin Israel mite ahin soldoh tan ahile, gamtepna lamlhun'na naicha ahi vang chun, Pathen'in Philistine galbol hojih chun lampia ahinpui pouvin ahi. Pathen'in aseiye, “Kamite hon galtoh khata le alung heikhao vintin Egypt lam'a kile ding ahiuve,” ati.
English: When Pharaoh had let the people go, God didn’t lead them by the way of the land of the Philistines, although that was near; for God said, “Lest perhaps the people change their minds when they see war, and they return to Egypt”;

EXO 14:6
Thadou: Pharaoh in jong agalsat miho le sakol kangtalai hochu agon tupsah loijin ahi.
English: He prepared his chariot, and took his army with him;

EXO 16:2
Thadou: Hiche mun jeng ajong chun Isreal mite Mose le Aaron heng'a aphunchil taovin ahi.
English: The whole congregation of the children of Israel murmured against Moses and against Aaron in the wilderness;

EXO 19:5
Thadou: Chule tua hi kathu nangai uva kakitepna nakoi jing uva ahileh, nangho hi vannoi mite jouse lah'a keima dia atumbeh'a naum diu; ajeh chu vannoi leiset pumpi hi keima'a ahi.”
English: Now therefore, if you will indeed obey my voice and keep my covenant, then you shall be my own possession from among all peoples; for all the earth is mine;

EXO 20:10
Thadou: Ni sagi lhinni hi na-Pakaiya dia cholngah nikho, hiche nikhoa hi nangman natoh ima nabol louhel ding chule nangma nahin, nachapa, nachanu, na sohpa, na sohnu, na gancha jouse le na kelkot phung hungsung lha'a na kholjin mi naboncha uva ima natoh thei lou hel diuva ahiye.”
English: but the seventh day is a Sabbath to the LORD your God. You shall not do any work in it, you, nor your son, nor your daughter, your male servant, nor your female servant, nor your livestock, nor your stranger who is within your gates;

EXO 21:18
Thadou: “Tun, Pasal khat le pasal khat akinah a, khatpan jong khat pachu song tum'a asuh ham akhut tumma akhet hamma ahile hiche amisuh pachu thipei dehlouva ahile jalkhun anga ding ahi.”
English: “If men quarrel and one strikes the other with a stone, or with his fist, and he doesn’t die, but is confined to bed;

EXO 22:10
Thadou: Tun tekahnan mi khat touvin aheng akom khat ngansena aneija sangan ahilou le bongchal ham kelngoi ham gancha khat pen pen apeh a ahile, hichu koima muphah nalou munkhat'a akidel mang tai.”
English: “If a man delivers to his neighbor a donkey, an ox, a sheep, or any animal to keep, and it dies or is injured, or driven away, no man seeing it;

EXO 22:23
Thadou: Amaho na suhgim uva ahile amaho ka heng lama hung diu chuteng keiman amaho taona ka san ding ahi, ati.
English: If you take advantage of them at all, and they cry at all to me, I will surely hear their cry;

EXO 25:32
Thadou: Thaomei phung ajet le avei apat abah gup hung um doh ding, thaomei pang lang khat a abah thum hung um doh ding chule khat lang'a ma chu abah thum hung kisep doh ding ahi.
English: There shall be six branches going out of its sides: three branches of the lamp stand out of its one side, and three branches of the lamp stand out of its other side;

EXO 25:33
Thadou: Hiche abah khat cheh apat chu thingga jom'a kisem doh bang'a khon thum chule aluchang umdoh ding, hichea pahcha jouse jong jaonan, hiti chun thaomei phung'a kon chun abah ahung jam doh'in ahi.
English: three cups made like almond blossoms in one branch, a bud and a flower; and three cups made like almond blossoms in the other branch, a bud and a flower, so for the six branches going out of the lamp stand;

EXO 25:34
Thadou: Thaomei khomjong chu thingga ajom bang bang'a kisem khon li ahin alulam jaonan apahcha jouse chutoh ajao vin ahi.
English: and in the lamp stand four cups made like almond blossoms, its buds and its flowers;

EXO 28:17
Thadou: A kimlaija gol lia song na gol ding chule amasa'a na gol ding chengse chu Sardis song hiding; Topaz song aiha song jong hiding ahi.
English: You shall set in it settings of stones, four rows of stones: a row of ruby, topaz, and beryl shall be the first row;

EXO 28:18
Thadou: Gol nina a pang ding hochu ahile, Emerald Song, sapphire song chule diamond song hiding ahi.
English: and the second row a turquoise, a sapphire, and an emerald;

EXO 28:19
Thadou: Gol thum lhinna pang ding hochu ahile; Jacinth song, Agate song chule Amethyst songhi ding ahi.
English: and the third row a jacinth, an agate, and an amethyst;

EXO 29:39
Thadou: Kelngoinou chu jingkah simma na kat doh jing ding chule kelngoinou dang khat chu nilhah lang a na kat doh ji ji ding ahi.
English: The one lamb you shall offer in the morning; and the other lamb you shall offer at evening;

EXO 30:23
Thadou: Nangman gimnamtui lah a anam tuipen na kilah ding, gimnam tui atwi lah Myrrh chu shekel ja-nga man nalah ding agim nam tui lah a ahoipen thingnam tuichu kehkhat nalah ding, hichu shekel jani le somnga alhing in, thingnam tui lah a jong anam twipen shekel jani le somnga mama nalah ding ahiye.
English: “Also take fine spices: of liquid myrrh, five hundred shekels; and of fragrant cinnamon half as much, even two hundred and fifty; and of fragrant cane, two hundred and fifty;

EXO 33:22
Thadou: “Ka loupina ahung kitol teng le keiman songpi kikah a kasel ding, hiche laimunna chu kasel jing ding keiman kadalhah teng le bou kahoh doh kit ding ahi,” ati.
English: It will happen, while my glory passes by, that I will put you in a cleft of the rock, and will cover you with my hand until I have passed by;

EXO 34:12
Thadou: “Tun nangma ki cheh theiyin, na chenna gammite toh kitepna hinsem khan nate, achuti louva ahile hitabang kitepna chu kipal lhuh'na hung pang ding ahi,” ati.
English: Be careful, lest you make a covenant with the inhabitants of the land where you are going, lest it be for a snare among you;

EXO 34:13
Thadou: “Hijeh chun nangman hiche gammite maicham jouse chu nasuh set gamhel ding, akhompi jouseo jong nasuh lhuh soh kei ding ahi, chule Asher doi jong chu na phuh lhuh ding ahi.”
English: but you shall break down their altars, and dash in pieces their pillars, and you shall cut down their Asherah poles;

EXO 34:15
Thadou: “Hijeh chun agamsung chengte toh kitepna na sem thei lou ding, hiche mite chun a pathen'nu umchan atho diu amaho le amho kah a jonthan hoi in apat diu, hiche pathen semthu ho heng'a kilhaina asem teng ule nangma jong nahin tep diu ahin, hiche a na hinkou pen pen-sa ki lhaina chu naneh thei lou ding ahi,” ati.
English: “Don’t make a covenant with the inhabitants of the land, lest they play the prostitute after their gods, and sacrifice to their gods, and one call you and you eat of his sacrifice;

EXO 35:8
Thadou: “Thaomei ding'a Olive thao hi ding; chule kinu ding thao namtui jong halnam thei thao twi jao cheh cheh ding ahi;
English: oil for the light, spices for the anointing oil and for the sweet incense,

EXO 35:11
Thadou: “A ponbuh ding, a chung vum'a khu ding, athil manchah jouse jao nan, ajol le akhompi jouse jaona hiding ahi;
English: the tabernacle, its outer covering, its roof, its clasps, its boards, its bars, its pillars, and its sockets;

EXO 35:12
Thadou: “Thingkong chule aputna ding moljol teni jong; hepi touna, chule pon akhu khumna'a kimang jong hi ding ahiye;
English: the ark, and its poles, the mercy seat, the veil of the screen;

EXO 35:13
Thadou: “Chule dokhang ahin amol jol ho jaona; manchah chengse le changlhah ki kat dohsa ho jaona hi ding ahi;
English: the table with its poles and all its vessels, and the show bread;

EXO 35:14
Thadou: “Meivah thaomei khom le aman chah chengse; chule Olive thao vahding jaona hi ding ahi.
English: the lamp stand also for the light, with its vessels, its lamps, and the oil for the light;

EXO 35:15
Thadou: Gimnam tui lhut na ding; chule amol jol chengse kinu ding; thaotwi le halnam thei thao twi chengse jong; chule houbuh a manchah ding pondal chengse jong hiding ahi.
English: and the altar of incense with its poles, the anointing oil, the sweet incense, the screen for the door, at the door of the tabernacle;

EXO 35:16
Thadou: Pumgo thilto maicham; chule athil keo Jouse kisilna kong le atunna jong ahi;
English: the altar of burnt offering, with its grating of bronze, its poles, and all its vessels, the basin and its base;

EXO 35:17
Thadou: Amunna khai ding ho jong; akhailhah nading khom ho jaonan; chule kotbulla khai ding pon dal jong jaona hiding ahiye.
English: the hangings of the court, its pillars, their sockets, and the screen for the gate of the court;

EXO 35:18
Thadou: Houbuh kilmat na ding ahom ho ahin, akhao jouse jong jao cheh ding ahi.
English: the pins of the tabernacle, the pins of the court, and their cords;

EXO 35:27
Thadou: Japi lamkaija pang chengse'n jong konggah ding le omphoa beh ding'in songman tam jatchom cheh ahin choi khom uvin ahi.
English: The rulers brought the onyx stones and the stones to be set for the ephod and for the breastplate;

EXO 35:31
Thadou: Pakaiyin Bezalel chu Pathen lhagao adimset sah jeng tan, amapa jong Chihna, le lung thim hat tah thil bol thei tah ahung hidoh tan ahi.”
English: He has filled him with the Spirit of God, in wisdom, in understanding, in knowledge, and in all kinds of workmanship;

EXO 36:37
Thadou: Chule aman ponbuh kot phung lam'a pansa ding chun adum, asan dup, asa-ao chule tupat pon jeng'a ajem in ahi.
English: He made a screen for the door of the tent, of blue, purple, scarlet, and fine twined linen, the work of an embroiderer;

EXO 37:20
Thadou: Hiche thaomei khom chu almond pahbang'in aning li aum'in ahi.
English: In the lamp stand were four cups made like almond blossoms, its buds and its flowers;

EXO 38:9
Thadou: Chuin Bezalel'in pal agen kimsoh keiyin, pal'a khaiding poun jouse chu tupat pomnem ma kisem jeng ahi. Chule lhanglam'a khai ding poundal se chu feet jakhat to somnga alhing'in ahi. hiche pal lhanglama khaiding pondal chengse jong chutupat ponnem jing a kikhong ahin agom chun tong jakhat jen ahilhng e.
English: He made the court: for the south side southward the hangings of the court were of fine twined linen, one hundred cubits;

EXO 38:14
Thadou: Kelkot polam'a pondal khat chu Tong somnileni akeh alhing in, chule atunna khom jong thum ahi.
English: the hangings for the one side were fifteen cubits; their pillars three, and their sockets three;

EXO 39:10
Thadou: Amahon song-mantam chu golli'n akoi jun. Amasan Carnelian song-san apansah'uvin, pale-green, chule emerald song ahi.
English: They set in it four rows of stones. A row of ruby, topaz, and beryl was the first row;

EXO 39:11
Thadou: Golni channa ding'in blue lapis lazuli, chule songgil ahi.
English: and the second row, a turquoise, a sapphire, and an emerald;

EXO 39:12
Thadou: Gol-thum channa ding'in aiha song, khipi chule umbel song ahi.
English: and the third row, a jacinth, an agate, and an amethyst;

EXO 39:25
Thadou: Chuin amahon sana thengsel'in chaojang asem'uvin hichengse chu abonchan kolbuthei jem le sangkhol golla chun akoiyun ahi.
English: They made bells of pure gold, and put the bells between the pomegranates around the skirts of the robe, between the pomegranates;

EXO 39:34
Thadou: Ponbuh khuna ding chun kelngoi chule kel chal-vun; hichengsea chu khuding ahi;
English: the covering of rams’ skins dyed red, the covering of sea cow hides, the veil of the screen,

EXO 39:36
Thadou: Dokhang le thilkeo ho; chule changlhah thilto chengse jaona ahi;
English: the table, all its vessels, the show bread,

EXO 39:37
Thadou: Sana thengsel'a ki semdoh thaomei-khom chule thaomei-khon chengse jaona, amanchah chengse le athaotwi jong jaona ahi;
English: the pure lamp stand, its lamps, even the lamps to be set in order, all its vessels, the oil for the light,

EXO 39:40
Thadou: Bangpheija kigol pondal ho; pal khom chengse ahin; chule houbuh lutna lam; houbuh'a kimang thil-le-lo jouse jaona ahi;
English: the hangings of the court, its pillars, its sockets, the screen for the gate of the court, its cords, its pins, and all the instruments of the service of the tabernacle, for the Tent of Meeting,

EXO 40:36
Thadou: Tun meibol jong chu houbuh akon'in ahung kitol tan ahile, Israel mite jeng jong meibol chie dungjuijin akitol tha jitauvin ahi.
English: When the cloud was taken up from over the tabernacle, the children of Israel went onward, throughout all their journeys;

LEV 1:7
Thadou: Hitia chu Aaron chapate thempu hon maicham chunga mei atikong diu, meikong chunga chu thing alom loma akoi diu ahi.
English: The sons of Aaron the priest shall put fire on the altar, and lay wood in order on the fire;

LEV 1:8
Thadou: Amahon maicham kitonaa sa kisem ho chu, aluchang leh athao hochu maicham chung meikou lah achu aban bana akoi diu ahi.
English: and Aaron’s sons, the priests, shall lay the pieces, the head, and the fat in order on the wood that is on the fire which is on the altar;

LEV 1:15
Thadou: Hiche teng chule thempu pan vapal leh vakhu ham chu maicham phunga akoi ding, chuteng aluchang chu maicham phung chunga atan lhah ding, thempupan amasa pena hiche thisan jouse chu maicham aning gol jousea achap khum ding ahi.
English: The priest shall bring it to the altar, and wring off its head, and burn it on the altar; and its blood shall be drained out on the side of the altar;

LEV 3:7
