Thadou: Chuin Gad leh Reuben chate Mose ang sung’a ahung lut tauvin, hiti hin asei uve, hiche muna hin kelngoinou tampi ka nei uvin, hijeh chun kelngoi kul ka sempeh uva, chule ka cha ka naote hou dinga jong chenna in phabep ka sah peh diu ahi.
English: They came near to him, and said, “We will build sheepfolds here for our livestock, and cities for our little ones;

NUM 32:26
Thadou: Ka chasen jouseu leh ka jite hou, kelngoite jouse abonchan Gilead khopi mun alha ngai diu ahi tai.
English: Our little ones, our wives, our flocks, and all our livestock shall be there in the cities of Gilead;

NUM 32:29
Thadou: Mose’n amaho henga hiti chun thu aseijin, Gad chate ahin Reuben chate abonchauva galmanchah choiya Pakai angsunga galsat dinga Jordan vadung agalkai soh kei uva, agam jeng jong hi Pakai angsunga ama thua anun a ahile, Gilead gam mun hi Amaho chen mun ding’a na peh doh jeng diu ahi.
English: Moses said to them, “If the children of Gad and the children of Reuben will pass with you over the Jordan, every man who is armed to battle before the LORD, and the land is subdued before you, then you shall give them the land of Gilead for a possession;

NUM 34:13
Thadou: Chuin Mose’n Israel chate henga hiti hin aseijin, Pakaiyin phungko leh phung kehkhat jaona mi apeh ding ahi tia kitepna a neisa chu hiche hi nangho jouse goulo ding’a kipe na hi tauve.
English: Moses commanded the children of Israel, saying, “This is the land which you shall inherit by lot, which the LORD has commanded to give to the nine tribes, and to the half-tribe;

