Thadou: Hiche gam pumpi chu ilo tauvin ahileh, keiman Reuben le Gad insung ading in Aroer apat Arnon Gorge changei in chule Gilead gam kehkhat le khopi phabep jaonan kapedoh tan ahi.
English: This land we took in possession at that time: from Aroer, which is by the valley of the Arnon, and half the hill country of Gilead with its cities, I gave to the Reubenites and to the Gadites;

DEU 3:16
Thadou: Chule keiman Reuben le Gad insunga ding in Gilead gam phabep jong kapen ahi. Arnon Gorge lhanglam lailung apat Ammon mite chenna Jabbok vadung chan ahi.
English: To the Reubenites and to the Gadites I gave from Gilead even to the valley of the Arnon, the middle of the valley, and its border, even to the river Jabbok, which is the border of the children of Ammon;

DEU 4:18
Thadou: tol-lhang lah a ganhing hihen, twipi noiya um ganhing limsem thu kitiphot angsunga na bohkhup lou diu ahi.
English: the likeness of anything that creeps on the ground, the likeness of any fish that is in the water under the earth;

DEU 4:21
Thadou: Hinlah nangho jeh in Pakai ka henga alungphamo tan. Pakaiyin kitepna asem in keima Jordan vadung galkaiya, keima hiche gamsunga khu kalut thei lou ding ahitai.
English: Furthermore the LORD was angry with me for your sakes, and swore that I should not go over the Jordan, and that I should not go in to that good land which the LORD your God gives you for an inheritance;

DEU 4:37
Thadou: Ajeh chu Pakaiyin napu napateu angailun chule a chilhahte changei phatthei aboh ahi. Pakaiyin abanthahat apan in, Egypt gam'a kona nahin pui galkaiyu ahitai.
English: Because he loved your fathers, therefore he chose their offspring after them, and brought you out with his presence, with his great power, out of Egypt;

DEU 4:47
Thadou: Chuin Israel miten Bashan lengpa Og lalna gam leh anei agou jouse achom chai keiyuvin, solama Amor mite leng teni jaona ahi.
English: They took possession of his land and the land of Og king of Bashan, the two kings of the Amorites, who were beyond the Jordan toward the sunrise;

DEU 5:13
Thadou: Natohna ding nigup naneiyun ahi,
English: You shall labor six days, and do all your work;

DEU 5:23
Thadou: Nanghon awgin le mu-athime ti najauvin chule molchung pumpi athimlha jeng tan ahileh, na insung cheh uva koin lamkaiho le upa ho ka henga ahung uvin ahi.
English: When you heard the voice out of the middle of the darkness, while the mountain was burning with fire, you came near to me, even all the heads of your tribes, and your elders;

DEU 6:1
Thadou: Pakai, Pathen in nangho seipeh dinga danthu eipeh hichengse hi ahi. Hiche gamsung nalut teng uleh, najui kimsoh kei diu ahi,
English: Now these are the commandments, the statutes, and the ordinances, which the LORD your God commanded to teach you, that you might do them in the land that you go over to possess;

DEU 6:6
Thadou: Tunia ka thupeh chengse aboncha chunga kipehna naneiyuva najui kimsoh kei diu ahi.
English: These words, which I command you today, shall be on your heart;

DEU 6:11
Thadou: Insung hoa chu neileh gou ijakai aki lamsa hi ding ahi. Twikul ho jong aki laisa ahin, Olive thing phung le adanghoa kona jong aga naneh diu, hicheho jouse hi nanghon tu lou hela aga nalo diu ahi. Hiche hohi naneh teng uleh gamsung pumpi nalodim diu ahitai.
English: and houses full of all good things which you didn’t fill, and cisterns dug out which you didn’t dig, vineyards and olive trees which you didn’t plant, and you shall eat and be full;

DEU 6:21
Thadou: Chuteng nanghon hitia hi na donbut diu, keiho Egypt gamsunga Pharaoh angsunga soh a kana um laiyuva Pakai, Pathen in abanthahat a eihin huh doh'u ahi.
English: then you shall tell your son, “We were Pharaoh’s slaves in Egypt. The LORD brought us out of Egypt with a mighty hand;

DEU 6:22
Thadou: Pakaiyin Egypt gamsunga Pharaoh le amite henga thil kidang ijakai aki lahsah in, ipu ipateu khanga pat akitepna gamsunga cheng dia eihin puiyu ahi.
English: and the LORD showed great and awesome signs and wonders on Egypt, on Pharaoh, and on all his house, before our eyes;

DEU 7:1
Thadou: Pakai, na Pathen uvin gam sunga nahin puilut teng uleh, nam dang tampi umho khu asuhmang ding ahi: Hit mite, Girgash mite, Amor mite, Canaan mite, Periz mite, Hiv mite le Jebus mite ahi. Hiche nam sagi hohi nang ho sanga hatjo le pungjo ahiuve.
English: When the LORD your God brings you into the land where you go to possess it, and casts out many nations before you—the Hittite, the Girgashite, the Amorite, the Canaanite, the Perizzite, the Hivite, and the Jebusite—seven nations greater and mightier than you;

DEU 7:7
Thadou: Pakaiyin namdang te banga thalhing le hatjo nahijeh uva nalhen tumu hilouvin, amavang nam neopen nahijeh uva nalhen joh’u ahi!
English: The LORD didn’t set his love on you nor choose you, because you were more in number than any people; for you were the fewest of all peoples;

DEU 8:7
Thadou: Ajeh chu Pakai, na Pathen uvin na gamu phatah twi nenna muna nahin puiyuva, hichu phaicham leh thing lhang gam aboncha ahi.
English: For the LORD your God brings you into a good land, a land of brooks of water, of springs, and underground water flowing into valleys and hills;

DEU 8:8
Thadou: Hiche gam pumpi hi mimchang le kolbu lei jeng ahin; theiba phung, kolbu thei phung, Olive phung leh khoiju lonna gam ahi.
English: a land of wheat, barley, vines, fig trees, and pomegranates; a land of olive trees and honey;

DEU 8:11
Thadou: Hinlah chingthei tah in um uvin! Ajeh chu hiche gampha laitah jeh a chu tunikhoa Pakai, na Pathen'u thupeh nasuh millou diu ahi.
English: Beware lest you forget the LORD your God, in not keeping his commandments, his ordinances, and his statutes, which I command you today;

DEU 8:12
Thadou: Nanghon innom nahin kisah doh diu chule haosatah a nain chen diu,
English: lest, when you have eaten and are full, and have built fine houses and lived in them;

DEU 8:13
Thadou: chule nagan chateu jong hung pung cheh cheh ding, sana leh dangka ijakai kimsela nahin neidiu chuteng chingthei tah naum diu ahi.
English: and when your herds and your flocks multiply, and your silver and your gold is multiplied, and all that you have is multiplied;

DEU 8:14
Thadou: Chutengleh kiletsah hoithona imacha naneilou diu ahi. Ajeh chu Egypt gamsunga gim genthei nathoh lai uva Pakai, Pathen in nahuh doh’u ahi.
English: then your heart might be lifted up, and you forget the LORD your God, who brought you out of the land of Egypt, out of the house of bondage;

DEU 8:15
Thadou: Pakaiyin gamthip noiya aipi hang leh gulse holah a nahin puidoh nau nagel doh jing diu, hiche mun chu tolgo lah le gamsa mun ahin, hinlah Pakaiyin twi nape uvin ahi.
English: who led you through the great and terrible wilderness, with venomous snakes and scorpions, and thirsty ground where there was no water; who poured water for you out of the rock of flint;

DEU 8:16
Thadou: Pakaiyin gamthip noiya manna in navah vaset uvin, hichu napu napateu khanga um khalou anneh ahi. Hiche hi Pakaiyin nangho patepna dinga abol ahin athua nanun cheh diu ahi.
English: who fed you in the wilderness with manna, which your fathers didn’t know, that he might humble you, and that he might prove you, to do you good at your latter end;

DEU 11:3
Thadou: Pakaiyin Egypt gam Pharaoh henga thil kidang tampi akilahsah in, hinlah amahon hichu amu hih laiyuve.
English: his signs, and his works, which he did in the middle of Egypt to Pharaoh the king of Egypt, and to all his land;

DEU 11:4
Thadou: Pakaiyin Egypt galsat miho le asakol kangtalai hou chunga itobanga na-atoh ham ti amu pouvin, chule Egypt miten nahindal laitah uva Twipi San dunga Pakai natoh jong amunai pouvin ahi. Amaho chu Pakaiyin asumang hel tauve.
English: and what he did to the army of Egypt, to their horses, and to their chariots; how he made the water of the Red Sea to overflow them as they pursued you, and how the LORD has destroyed them to this day;

DEU 11:5
Thadou: Gamthip akon tuni chanin Pakaiyin, ichangeiya nakhohsah uham ti nachateu vin amu nai pouve.
English: and what he did to you in the wilderness until you came to this place;

DEU 11:6
Thadou: Reuben chilhah, Eliab chapa teni Dathan leh Abiram chunga Pathen natoh jong nachaten amu pouvin ahi. Gamleiset Israel mite chenna aki hoh in, chuin amaho abonchauvin agam hel tauvin; aponbuh hou ahin chule anei leh agou ganchahou, jaonan abonchan amang heltan ahi.
English: and what he did to Dathan and Abiram, the sons of Eliab, the son of Reuben—how the earth opened its mouth and swallowed them up, with their households, their tents, and every living thing that followed them, in the middle of all Israel;

DEU 11:8
Thadou: Hijeh chun chingtheiyun, tunia thupeh chengse aboncha najui kimsoh keidiu ahi. Chutileh na thahat diu nalhunna diu gamsung nalo thei diu ahi.
English: Therefore you shall keep the entire commandment which I command you today, that you may be strong, and go in and possess the land that you go over to possess;

DEU 11:10
Thadou: Hiche gam naluodiu khu nahin dalhah’u Egypt gam tobang ahipon, hiche gam leiset achun hon sunga ipi muchi hijongleh aga aphapon ahi.
English: For the land, where you go in to possess isn’t like the land of Egypt that you came out of, where you sowed your seed and watered it with your foot, as a garden of herbs;

DEU 11:16
Thadou: Hinlah chingtheiyun. Na lungthim'u phat mosah hih uvin, ajeh chu Pakai, Pathen akona Pathen dang nabel lo diu ahi.
English: Be careful, lest your heart be deceived, and you turn away to serve other gods and worship them;

DEU 11:20
Thadou: Thupeh chengse chu kot phung leh kelkot jousea najih diu ahi.
English: You shall write them on the door posts of your house and on your gates;

DEU 11:27
Thadou: Pakai, na Pathen'u thupeh chengse hi na nitsoh keiyuva ahileh, nangho phatthei na chan diu ahi.
English: the blessing, if you listen to the commandments of the LORD your God, which I command you today;

DEU 12:8
Thadou: Pakai kin nabol danu jong kikhel ding ahi. Tunin nabon chauvin natao uve.
English: You shall not do all the things that we do here today, every man whatever is right in his own eyes;

DEU 12:13
Thadou: Nangho chingtheiyun, ajeh chu mun jousea pumgo thilto na katdoh thei lou diu ahi.
English: Be careful that you don’t offer your burnt offerings in every place that you see;

DEU 12:17
Thadou: Hinlah nanghon na thilto hou chu na khopi sung uva naneh thei lou diu, hichu soma khat ahin, gathah, Olive thao, nagancha asoh masaho ahin chule kitepna thilto, chule mimal kipehna thilto ho hijongleh khopi dunga naneh thang lou diu ahi.
English: You may not eat within your gates the tithe of your grain, or of your new wine, or of your oil, or the firstborn of your herd or of your flock, nor any of your vows which you vow, nor your free will offerings, nor the wave offering of your hand;

DEU 13:6
Thadou: Mikhat touvin guhthima nahin lhep diu nasopipa, nachanu ham nachapa, nangailuttah najinu, ahilouleh naloi ngaipen najah uva hitia hi asei diu, ‘pathen dang hou din cheu hite ati diu, hinlah hiche pathen hohi napu, na pateu jeng in jong ana het khah lou ahi.
English: If your brother, the son of your mother, or your son, or your daughter, or the wife of your bosom, or your friend who is as your own soul, entices you secretly, saying, “Let’s go and serve other gods”—which you have not known, you, nor your fathers;

DEU 13:8
Thadou: Hinlah athu uva nanun louhel diu ahi. Chule hepina jong nanei lou diu, ven jong naven bit thei lou hel diu ahi.
English: you shall not consent to him nor listen to him; neither shall your eye pity him, neither shall you spare, neither shall you conceal him;

DEU 15:7
Thadou: Hinlah Pakai, na Pathen uvin napehnau gam nalhun tenguleh, Israel insunga kona avaicha aum khah leh amachu nadal bol lou hel diu ahi.
English: If a poor man, one of your brothers, is with you within any of your gates in your land which the LORD your God gives you, you shall not harden your heart, nor shut your hand from your poor brother;

DEU 16:5
Thadou: Hiche kut hi khopi tinchenga nabol thei lou diu ahi.
English: You may not sacrifice the Passover within any of your gates which the LORD your God gives you;

DEU 17:19
Thadou: Hiche danbu lekhajol chu akoma akoi ding adamlai sunga asim jing ding ahi. Hichea kona chu dan leh thupeh ijakai Pakaiya kon in aume ti amu chet ding, dengchang tah’a ajui jing ding ahi.
English: It shall be with him, and he shall read from it all the days of his life, that he may learn to fear the LORD his God, to keep all the words of this law and these statutes, to do them;

DEU 19:8
