English: The king called the Gibeonites and said to them (now the Gibeonites were not of the children of Israel, but of the remnant of the Amorites, and the children of Israel had sworn to them; and Saul sought to kill them in his zeal for the children of Israel and Judah);

2SA 21:8
Thadou: Chuin lengpan Aiah chanu Saul jinu Rizpah chapate ni Armoni le Mephibosheth amanin, Saul chanu Merab chapate mi nga jong amanin, amaho hi Merab hin Meholath mipa Barzillai chapa Adriel kitipa chutoh ahinlhon ahi;
English: But the king took the two sons of Rizpah the daughter of Aiah, whom she bore to Saul, Armoni and Mephibosheth; and the five sons of Merab the daughter of Saul, whom she bore to Adriel the son of Barzillai the Meholathite.

2SA 21:12
Thadou: David jong achen Saul leh achapa Jonathan gu-lheng lhon chengse beh chu Jabesh-gilead kho haosate koma agalan ahi. Chule hiche haosa hohin, hiche gu-lheng lhon ho hi Philistine miten Gilboa molsang chunga Saul ajo chung uva, Philistine mihon Saul leh achapa Jonathan Beth-shan kholai dunga akhai nauva aga guh doh-u anahi.
English: So David went and took the bones of Saul and the bones of Jonathan his son from the men of Jabesh Gilead, who had stolen them from the street of Beth Shan, where the Philistines had hanged them in the day that the Philistines killed Saul in Gilboa;

2SA 21:15
Thadou: Hichun Philistine mite chun Israel chate dounan gal ahinbol uvin ahileh, David lengpa jong chu asepaite toh kilhonin gal akonsuh kit’in Philistine mite dounan gal agasat tauve. Hichun David jong chu atha achol lheh jengin ahi.
English: The Philistines had war again with Israel; and David went down, and his servants with him, and fought against the Philistines. David grew faint;

2SA 22:2
Thadou: Hitin lacheng aseme, “Pakai chu keima dingin Kasongpi leh kakulpi chule eihuhhingpa ahi,
English: and he said: “The LORD is my rock, my fortress, and my deliverer, even mine;

2SA 22:5
Thadou: “Ajeh chu thina luipin eilon khuntan, Manthah na lam jousen eilon khum tai;
English: For the waves of death surrounded me. The floods of ungodliness made me afraid.

2SA 23:16
Thadou: Hichun hiche mihat mithumho hin Philistinete ngahmun kimlai tah chu atum keh jenguvin Bethlehem khopi kulpi kelkot phunga twikula twi chu agathal’uvin, David henga ahin dop peh tauve. Ahin David chun donjo talouvin atwi chu Pakai lhai nan tol'a asung lhan;
English: The three mighty men broke through the army of the Philistines, and drew water out of the well of Bethlehem that was by the gate and took it and brought it to David; but he would not drink of it, but poured it out to the LORD.

2SA 24:5
Thadou: Chuin amahon amasapen in Jordan vadung chu apal galkaiyun lhanglam khopi phaicham, Aroer khopi Gad lam jot na ah chun aponbuh asongun,chujou vin Jazer langa achi pei taove.
English: They passed over the Jordan and encamped in Aroer, on the right side of the city that is in the middle of the valley of Gad, and to Jazer;

1KI 1:9
Thadou: Adonijah chun En-royal twinah komma Zoheleth song phunga chun ache in chule hilai mun ah chun kelngoiho, bongchal ho leh bongnou thaotah tah ho mangchan pumgo thilto ana boltan ahi. Hichea chun David lengpa chapate, a sopi ho chengse ho leh Judahh gamsung’a Lengpa ding’a pan mun neiho jouse jong ana koukhom in ahi.
English: Adonijah killed sheep, cattle, and fatlings by the stone of Zoheleth, which is beside En Rogel; and he called all his brothers, the king’s sons, and all the men of Judah, the king’s servants;

1KI 2:2
Thadou: “Keima hi Leiset chung’a um mihem jouse phatkhat leh ache cheh na diu mun chu kajot ding ahitai. Nangman hangsan tah in pasal phatah umchan hin th in,
English: “I am going the way of all the earth. You be strong therefore, and show yourself a man;

1KI 4:2
Thadou: Hitichun ama ding’a vaihom a pang ho jouse chu hicheng hi ahiuve: Zadok chapa Azariah chu thempun apang in,
English: These were the princes whom he had: Azariah the son of Zadok, the priest;

1KI 4:3
Thadou: Shisha chapa teni Elihoreph leh Ahijah chu lekha sun in apang lhon in, Ahilud chapa Jehosaphat chu thusimbu ching in apang in ahi,
English: Elihoreph and Ahijah, the sons of Shisha, scribes; Jehoshaphat the son of Ahilud, the recorder;

1KI 4:4
Thadou: Jehoiada chapa Benaiah chu sepaite lamkaijin apang in, Zadok le Abiather chu Thempun apang lhonne,
English: Benaiah the son of Jehoiada was over the army; Zadok and Abiathar were priests;

1KI 4:5
Thadou: Chu jong leh Azariah kitipa Nathan chapa chu Gambeh gam vaipo ho jouse chunga vaihom in apang’e, Nathan themgao chapa Zabud chu lengpa thumop in apang in ahi,
English: Azariah the son of Nathan was over the officers; Zabud the son of Nathan was chief minister, the king’s friend;

1KI 4:8
Thadou: Hiche gamvaipo som le ni ho minchu hiche ho hi ahiuve: Ephraim thing lhang a cheng Benhur,
English: These are their names: Ben Hur, in the hill country of Ephraim;

1KI 4:9
Thadou: Bendeker hin Makaz, Shaalbim, Beth-shemesh leh Elon-bethhanan apoh ahi,
English: Ben Deker, in Makaz, in Shaalbim, Beth Shemesh, and Elon Beth Hanan;

1KI 4:10
Thadou: Ben-hased in Arubboth leh Socoh chuleh Hepher gam jong apoh ahi.
English: Ben Hesed, in Arubboth (Socoh and all the land of Hepher belonged to him);

1KI 4:11
Thadou: Ben-abinadab in Naphoth-dor (Ama hin Solomon chanu khat Taphath kitinu chu a kichen pi ahi).
English: Ben Abinadab, in all the height of Dor (he had Taphath, Solomon’s daughter, as wife);

1KI 4:12
Thadou: Ahilud chapa Baana in Taanach le Magiddo, Jezreel noiya um Zerethan komma Bethshan pumpi apon, chuleh Bethshan apat Abel-meholah kikah gam pumpi Jokmeam chung lang jong apon ahi.
English: Baana the son of Ahilud, in Taanach and Megiddo, and all Beth Shean which is beside Zarethan, beneath Jezreel, from Beth Shean to Abel Meholah, as far as beyond Jokmeam;

1KI 4:13
Thadou: Ben-geber in Ramoth-gilead le Gilead na Jeir khopi ho pum in apon (Jair kitihi Manasseh phung ahi), chuleh Bashan a Argob gamkol jong apon, chuleh sum eng kelkot kiget khum leh kulpi kikai khum khopi lentah cheh somgup jong apohtha’n ahi.
English: Ben Geber, in Ramoth Gilead (the towns of Jair the son of Manasseh, which are in Gilead, belonged to him; and the region of Argob, which is in Bashan, sixty great cities with walls and bronze bars, belonged to him);

1KI 4:14
Thadou: Iddo chapa Ahinadab in Mahanaim apon,
English: Ahinadab the son of Iddo, in Mahanaim;

1KI 4:15
Thadou: Ahimaaz in Naphtali apon (Ama hin Solomon chanu lah a khat Basemath chu akichen pin ahi).
English: Ahimaaz, in Naphtali (he also took Basemath the daughter of Solomon as wife);

1KI 4:16
Thadou: Hushai chapa Banna in Asher leh Aloth apon,
English: Baana the son of Hushai, in Asher and Bealoth;

1KI 4:17
Thadou: Paruah chapa Jehoshaphat in Issachar apon,
English: Jehoshaphat the son of Paruah, in Issachar;

1KI 4:18
Thadou: Ela chapa Shimei in Benjamin apon,
English: Shimei the son of Ela, in Benjamin;

1KI 7:28
Thadou: Hiche kangtalai ho chu kolbem a kisem ahin chule amaitom cheh aneiyun ahi, hiche amai tom cheh u chu akolsunga kitung cheh ahi.
English: The work of the bases was like this: they had panels; and there were panels between the ledges;

1KI 7:41
Thadou: Khompi teni ahin, khompi teni tomna dinga alujum kisem teni ahin chule alujum leiteni tomna dinga sum-eng chaokol jilla kijil teni ahin, lenchapeh a kipheh khompi teni lutomna kimang teni jong ahin,
English: the two pillars; the two bowls of the capitals that were on the top of the pillars; the two networks to cover the two bowls of the capitals that were on the top of the pillars;

1KI 7:42
Thadou: Lencha pheh banga kipheh teni dinga kisem kolbuthei pah tobang jali jen ahin, khompi teni lutomna ding’a kibol Lencha pheh banga ki pheh khat cheh a pang dia golni’a ding kol buthei pah kisem cheng se chu toh ahi.
English: the four hundred pomegranates for the two networks; two rows of pomegranates for each network, to cover the two bowls of the capitals that were on the pillars;

1KI 7:43
Thadou: Khomtodal chengse ahin khomtodal chunga pang ding tuibel som jong ahi.
English: the ten bases; the ten basins on the bases;

1KI 7:44
Thadou: Chujongle tuikong khat ahin, hiche tuikong kisem noija chun bongchal somleni lim akiseme.
English: the one sea; the twelve oxen under the sea;

1KI 7:48
Thadou: Solomon in Pakai houin sunga manchah ding thil le lo asem chengse chu hicheng hi ahi, sana maicham ahin, kilhaina ding changlhah todoh na ding dokhang ahin,
English: Solomon made all the vessels that were in the LORD’s house: the golden altar and the table that the show bread was on, of gold;

1KI 7:49
Thadou: Sana thengsella kisem thaomei khom ahin, insung dan mun theng maija akitung in lhanglam ngan abah nga akitung in, sahlam ngan bah nga ma aki tung’e, pahcha lim kisemle thaomei ho ahin, cheiche chengse chutoh ahin, sana jong ahiuve.
English: and the lamp stands, five on the right side and five on the left, in front of the inner sanctuary, of pure gold; and the flowers, the lamps, and the tongs, of gold;

1KI 8:22
Thadou: Hijou chun, Solomon chu Israel mipite jouse masang Pakai maicham noija chun adingin, vanlam’ah akhut adom sang in,
English: Solomon stood before the LORD’s altar in the presence of all the assembly of Israel, and spread out his hands toward heaven;

1KI 8:23
Thadou: Hitin atao tai, “Vo Pakai Israel Pathen, hiche vannoi leiset ahin nang tobang Pathen dang aum poi, Nang ma mitmu’a alung thim pumpia kal songho chung ah na kitepna dung juiyin na ngailut na lhasam louhel in na musah jing in ahi.
English: and he said, “LORD, the God of Israel, there is no God like you, in heaven above, or on earth beneath; who keeps covenant and loving kindness with your servants who walk before you with all their heart;

1KI 8:28
Thadou: Ahinlah, O Pakai ka Pathen kataona le kathum nahi nei ngaipeh in, na sohpa na kom’a kaka nale ka taona hi nei ngai peh tei jin,
English: Yet have respect for the prayer of your servant and for his supplication, LORD my God, to listen to the cry and to the prayer which your servant prays before you today;

1KI 8:39
Thadou: Hiteng chule na chenna van gam a konin hin ngaidam in. Namite hin achonna’u dung jui'a achan diuva lom chu pe jengin, ajeh chu nang in mi lungthim jouse jong nahetsohkei sa ahi.
English: then hear in heaven, your dwelling place, and forgive, and act, and give to every man according to all his ways, whose heart you know (for you, even you only, know the hearts of all the children of men);

1KI 8:46
Thadou: “Amahon nangma douna ahung chonset jeng uva ahileh koihi achonse khalou um am? Nangma jeng jong nalung hanga agalmiteu na josah thei ahilouleh agal miteuvin agam uva gal hing’a na kaimang sahthei jong ahi.
English: If they sin against you (for there is no man who doesn’t sin), and you are angry with them and deliver them to the enemy, so that they carry them away captive to the land of the enemy, far off or near;

1KI 8:49
Thadou: Hiteng chuleh na chenna vanna konin atao nau chu hin ngai inlang ahahsatna’u hinvet peh tei jin.
English: then hear their prayer and their supplication in heaven, your dwelling place, and maintain their cause;

1KI 8:51
Thadou: Ajeh chu amaho namite Egypt meibang’a sa thohgim na akona na hin puidoh na deilhen nam mite ahiuve.
English: (for they are your people and your inheritance, which you brought out of Egypt, from the middle of the iron furnace);

1KI 8:59
Thadou: Chuleh Pakai anga tunia ka taona thucheng hohi asun ajan in a-angsung’a ging jing hen, hitia chu ami Israel te hi nitin i-ngaichat dung jui uva thu dih’a eipui theina diuvin.
English: Let these my words, with which I have made supplication before the LORD, be near to the LORD our God day and night, that he may maintain the cause of his servant and the cause of his people Israel, as every day requires;

1KI 12:2
Thadou: Nebat chapa Jeroboam chun hichu ajah phat in Egypt’a konin ahung kile tan ahi. Ama chu Solomon lengpa a kona Egypt achu ana jamlut na ahi.
English: When Jeroboam the son of Nebat heard of it (for he was yet in Egypt, where he had fled from the presence of King Solomon, and Jeroboam lived in Egypt;

1KI 13:8
Thadou: Pathen mipan Lengpa kom achun, “Na lenggam akeh khat neipeh ding hi jong leh nang toh kilhon khom pong’e, keiman hiche mun’a hi nehle chah kahol lou ding ahi,
English: The man of God said to the king, “Even if you gave me half of your house, I would not go in with you, neither would I eat bread nor drink water in this place;

1KI 13:20
Thadou: Hitia chu amani atou khompet lhon chun Pakaija konin Themgao tehsepu kom achun thupeh khat ahung lhung tan ahile,
English: As they sat at the table, the LORD’s word came to the prophet who brought him back;

1KI 14:25
Thadou: Rehoboam lengpa vaihom kum nga chan in Egypt lengpa Shishak chun Jerusalem ahin nokhum in ahi.
English: In the fifth year of King Rehoboam, Shishak king of Egypt came up against Jerusalem;

1KI 15:4
Thadou: Ahin David jal’a, Pakai Pathen in achilhahte aban banna thaomeivah banga vah dinga vaihomna mun ahin ban losah ahin, achapa Abijah jong chu ama nunga Jerusalema vai ahin hop sah ahi.
English: Nevertheless for David’s sake, the LORD his God gave him a lamp in Jerusalem, to set up his son after him and to establish Jerusalem;

1KI 15:29
Thadou: Aman Jeroboam chilhahte abonchan ana that gamin, leng insunga mite chu khatcha ana hinghoi pon ahi. Hichehi Pakaiyin Shiloh’a, Ahijah Themgaopa mangcha a Jeroboam chung chang thu ana sei chu aguilhun na ahi tai.
English: As soon as he was king, he struck all the house of Jeroboam. He didn’t leave to Jeroboam any who breathed, until he had destroyed him, according to the saying of the LORD, which he spoke by his servant Ahijah the Shilonite;

1KI 16:9
Thadou: Hijouchun lengte galsatna sakol kangtalai ho akehkhat chung’a lamkai Zimri chun ama chu tha ding ana gongin ahi. Tirzah khopia nikhat hi Elah chu khopi sung vaipopa Arza insung a ju ana kham in,
English: His servant Zimri, captain of half his chariots, conspired against him. Now he was in Tirzah, drinking himself drunk in the house of Arza, who was over the household in Tirzah;

1KI 18:3
Thadou: Hijeh chun Ahab chun khopi vesuija pang Obadiah chu ana kouvin ahi. Amachu chu Pakai nungjui dih tah ahi.
English: Ahab called Obadiah, who was over the household. (Now Obadiah feared the LORD greatly;

1KI 20:5
Thadou: Benhadad in gangtah in adonbutna thu chu athot kit in, “Hiche Benhadad keima thuthot ahi, na sana leh na dangka chu leh naji na chate neipeh ding ahi tia, thu kapehsa nahitai.
English: The messengers came again and said, “Ben Hadad says, ‘I sent indeed to you, saying, “You shall deliver me your silver, your gold, your wives, and your children;

2KI 9:14
Thadou: Nimshi chapa Jehoshaphat chapa Jehu chun Joram lengpa dounan gal aboltan ahi. Joram hi Ramoth a Gilead munna Israelte huhna dia Syria lengpa Hazael sepaite toh kidouva umma ahi.
English: So Jehu the son of Jehoshaphat the son of Nimshi conspired against Joram. (Now Joram was defending Ramoth Gilead, he and all Israel, because of Hazael king of Syria;

2KI 11:5
Thadou: Jehoiada chun amaho kom achun, “Nangho hop thumma naki khen uva, hopkhat cholngah nileh leng inpi ngah a napandiu ahi, hiche hi nabol teidiu ahi,” atipeh tan ahi.
English: He commanded them, saying, “This is what you must do: a third of you, who come in on the Sabbath, shall be keepers of the watch of the king’s house;

2KI 11:13
Thadou: Athaliah in, mipi hole leng inpi ngah ho husan chu ajahdoh phat’in, ipi thilsoh hitam? tin aveding in gangchal’in houin langa chun aga lhailut tan ahi.
English: When Athaliah heard the noise of the guard and of the people, she came to the people into the LORD’s house;

2KI 12:13
Thadou: Hiche sum, houin a hunglut hochu, houin sunga manchah ding kisilna dangka kong ahin, thaomeija manchah ding chaiche ahin, konglenho le khon ho ahin, sumkon chuleh san le dangka a kisem thil adang dang ho akisemnan khatcha akimang pon ahi.
English: But there were not made for the LORD’s house cups of silver, snuffers, basins, trumpets, any vessels of gold or vessels of silver, of the money that was brought into the LORD’s house;

2KI 17:9
Thadou: Israel mipi loikhat’in, Pakai a Pathen’u deiloulam le doumah thil tamtah aguh’a anabol jeh’u ahi. Amahon Pathen neiloute, doiphungho, khovetna mun neo apatna khopi pal lenpen chung geija amahon kisem doh’uva akitundoh’u ahi.
English: The children of Israel secretly did things that were not right against the LORD their God; and they built high places for themselves in all their cities, from the tower of the watchmen to the fortified city;

2KI 17:10
Thadou: Lhangvum dung jouse le thingnadum noi dung jousea doikhom hole Asherah doiphung ana kitun’un ahi.
English: and they set up for themselves pillars and Asherah poles on every high hill and under every green tree;

2KI 17:11
Thadou: Amahon namdangte maicham phung dung’a gimnamtui alhut nam’un, agamsung a Pakaiyin adeldohsa nam mite chonchan jouse ajom tauvin ahi. Hiti chun Israelten setna tampi anabollun, Pakai lung ahansah ji jin ahi.
English: and there they burned incense in all the high places, as the nations whom the LORD carried away before them did; and they did wicked things to provoke the LORD to anger;

2KI 17:34
Thadou: Hiche achondan lui hochu tunikho geijin achepiuvin ahi. Amahon Pakai chu ahoutah tah pouvin, amavang tumasang a achonnau chu ajui-nalaijun ahi. Amahon Pakaiyin Israel tia amin anakhelpeh Jacob chihlhahte anapeh thupeh hole ajuidiuva dan ana sempeh hochu khatcha jong ajui pouvin ahi.
English: To this day they do what they did before. They don’t fear the LORD, and they do not follow the statutes, or the ordinances, or the law, or the commandment which the LORD commanded the children of Jacob, whom he named Israel;

2KI 17:35
Thadou: Ajeh chu Pakaiyin Jacob chilhahte hochu kitepna ana semin, ajui diuvin thupeh hitin anapei, “Pathen dang hou hih’un ahilouleh a ang’a jong nakun theilou diu, jen-jong najen theilou diu, akom’uva jong kilhaina nabol theilou heldiu ahi,” ati.
English: with whom the LORD had made a covenant and commanded them, saying, “You shall not fear other gods, nor bow yourselves to them, nor serve them, nor sacrifice to them;

2KI 18:31
Thadou: Hezekiah thusei tahsan hih un, Assyria lengpan nangho napehnom’u kitepna chu hichehi ahi. Keitoh chamna sem’un, khopi kelkot hi hong’unlang hung potdoh’un. Achutileh nanghon nalengpithei’u leh nathei chang’u nakinehdiu, chuleh na tuikul uva nakidondiu ahi.
English: Don’t listen to Hezekiah.’ For the king of Assyria says, ‘Make your peace with me, and come out to me; and everyone of you eat from his own vine, and everyone from his own fig tree, and everyone drink water from his own cistern;

2KI 21:7
Thadou: Manasseh hin Asherah semthu pathen lim jeng jong ana sem’in, Pakaiyin David leh achapa Solomon anaseipeh na mun laitah houin sunga chun ana tungdoh in ahi. “Israel phungho jouse lah a kona kana lhendoh Jerusalem khopi leh a houin nahi kamin hi atonsot na kijajing ding ahi,” anati ahi.
English: He set the engraved image of Asherah that he had made in the house of which the LORD said to David and to Solomon his son, “In this house, and in Jerusalem, which I have chosen out of all the tribes of Israel, I will put my name forever;

2KI 21:11
Thadou: “Judahte lengpa Manasseh in thet um tahtah thil tamtah ana boldoh in ahi. Israelte hiche gam’a achenlut masang uva anacheng Amor mite sangin thilsejo ana boldoh in ahi. Aman Judah mitehi milim semthu doilim houna a ana chonset sah in ahi,” ati.
English: “Because Manasseh king of Judah has done these abominations, and has done wickedly above all that the Amorites did, who were before him, and has also made Judah to sin with his idols;

2KI 21:21
Thadou: Amahin apa Manasseh in anabolbang bangin Pakai mitmu’n thilse jing ana bollin ahi.
English: He walked in all the ways that his father walked in, and served the idols that his father served, and worshiped them;

2KI 23:22
Thadou: Israelten thutan vaihom ho khanglai apat’a Israel lengte khanglai le Judah lengte khanglai geija jong hitobang kalchuh kut hi ana kimang kha talou ahitai.
English: Surely there was not kept such a Passover from the days of the judges who judged Israel, nor in all the days of the kings of Israel, nor of the kings of Judah;

2KI 25:18
Thadou: Nebuzaradan sepai lamkaipa chun thempulen Seraiah le thempu ni lhinna Zephaniah kitipa chutoh kelkot ngah apangji mithum chutoh sohchang dingin akai mangin ahi.
English: The captain of the guard took Seraiah the chief priest, Zephaniah the second priest, and the three keepers of the threshold;

2KI 25:29
Thadou: Aman Jehoiachin chu songkul von khel chun vonthah anapen chuleh ahinkho lhung keija lengpatoh anneh khom dingin phalna anapen ahi.
English: and changed his prison garments. Jehoiachin ate bread before him continually all the days of his life;

1CH 1:1
Thadou: Adam son le achilhahho Seth, Enosh;
English: Adam, Seth, Enosh,

1CH 2:10
Thadou: Ram hin Amminadab ahingin, chule Amminadab hin Judahte leng chapa Nahshon ahingin ahi.
English: Ram became the father of Amminadab, and Amminadab became the father of Nahshon, prince of the children of Judah;

1CH 2:12
Thadou: Boaz chun Obed ahingin, Obed in Jesse ahinge.
English: and Boaz became the father of Obed, and Obed became the father of Jesse;

1CH 2:15
Thadou: Ozem chu achapa gup lhinna ahin, chule asagi lhinna chu David ahitai.
English: Ozem the sixth, and David the seventh;

1CH 3:1
Thadou: Hebron khopia achen laiya David in ahin achapate chu hicheng hi ahiuve: achapa apeng masapen chu Ammon ahin, apenna nu chu Ahinoam akitin Jezreel kho mi ahi. Achapa ni lhinna pachu Daniel ahin, Carmel kho numeinu Anogail toh ahinlhon ahi.
English: Now these were the sons of David, who were born to him in Hebron: the firstborn, Amnon, of Ahinoam the Jezreelitess; the second, Daniel, of Abigail the Carmelitess;

1CH 3:2
Thadou: Athum lhinna pachu Absalom ahin, anu chu Maacah akitin, Geshur lengpa Talmai chanu ahi. Li lhinna pachu Adonijah ahin, anu chu Haggith ahi.
English: the third, Absalom the son of Maacah the daughter of Talmai king of Geshur; the fourth, Adonijah the son of Haggith;

1CH 3:4
Thadou: Hebron khopia kum sagi le akeh khat sunga lengvaipoa anapan sungin David chun chapa gu hi anahingin ahi. Chujouvin kum som thumle kum thum sungin Jerusalem khopia lengvaipon anapangin ahi.
English: six were born to him in Hebron; and he reigned there seven years and six months. He reigned thirty-three years in Jerusalem;

1CH 3:5
Thadou: Jerusalem khopia achen laiya David in anahin achapate chu Shammua, Shobad, Nathan, chule Solomon ahiuve. Amaho penna nu chu Ammiel chanu Bathsheba ahi.
English: and these were born to him in Jerusalem: Shimea, Shobab, Nathan, and Solomon, four, by Bathshua the daughter of Ammiel;

1CH 3:19
Thadou: Pedaiah chapate ni chu Zerubbabel le Shimei ahilhone. Zerubbabel chapate ni chu Meshullam le Hananiah ahilhonin, Amani sopinu chu Shelomith akiti.
English: The sons of Pedaiah: Zerubbabel and Shimei. The sons of Zerubbabel: Meshullam and Hananiah; and Shelomith was their sister;

1CH 4:21
Thadou: Shelah kitipa hi Judah chapate ho lah’a mi khat anahi. Shelah son achilhah ho chu Lecah pa Er; Mareshah pa Laasah; chule Beth-Ashbea kho’a tupat pon khonga pang insung mite toh;
English: The sons of Shelah the son of Judah: Er the father of Lecah, Laadah the father of Mareshah, and the families of the house of those who worked fine linen, of the house of Ashbea;

1CH 4:24
Thadou: Simeon chapate chu Jemuel*, Jamin, Jarib, Zohar,* chule Shaul ahiuve.
English: The sons of Simeon: Nemuel, Jamin, Jarib, Zerah, Shaul;

1CH 4:32
Thadou: David lengvaipoa ahung pan masanga kho hijat hi amaho thuneina noiya um ngen ahiuve. Amaho son achilhah hochu Etam, Ain, Rimmon, Token, chule Ashan pumin khopi nga,
English: Their villages were Etam, Ain, Rimmon, Tochen, and Ashan, five cities;

1CH 5:7
Thadou: Beerah inkote chu ama phung sunga akhangguiya akisimtoh’a akijih toh tengleh ahaosa chu Jeriel ahin, Zechariah jong ahi;
English: His brothers by their families, when the genealogy of their generations was listed: the chief, Jeiel, and Zechariah,

1CH 5:8
Thadou: Chule Azaz chapa Bela ahin, Shema chapa ahin, chule Joel chapa jong ahi. Reuben mite ho hi Aroer apat Nebon changei, chule Baal-Meon chan geiya cheng ahiuve.
English: and Bela the son of Azaz, the son of Shema, the son of Joel, who lived in Aroer, even to Nebo and Baal Meon;

1CH 5:14
Thadou: Hiche ho chengse hi abonchauva Huri chapa Abihail son achilhah jeng ahiuve; Huri chu joroah chapa ahin, Joroah chu Gilead chapa ahin, Michael chu Jeshishai chapa ahin, Jeshishai chu Jahdo chapa, chule Jahdo chu Buz chapa ahi.
English: These were the sons of Abihail, the son of Huri, the son of Jaroah, the son of Gilead, the son of Michael, the son of Jeshishai, the son of Jahdo, the son of Buz;

1CH 6:39
Thadou: Heman’in manchah phapenna anei masapa Gershon chilhah miho lah’a Asaph kitipa chu Berekiah chapa ahin, Berekiah chu Shimea chapa ahi;
English: His brother Asaph, who stood on his right hand, even Asaph the son of Berechiah, the son of Shimea,

1CH 6:55
Thadou: Mihon amaho chu Judah gamsunga Hebron khopi le akimvel gamse se toh chule avel’a hamhing gam gancha vahna ding jouse chutoh apeh tha taove;
English: to them they gave Hebron in the land of Judah, and its pasture lands around it;

1CH 6:59
Thadou: Ain khoppi, Juttah khopi, chule Beth-Shemesh khopi toh hichengse hi ahi.
English: Ashan with its pasture lands, and Beth Shemesh with its pasture lands;

1CH 7:28
Thadou: Ephraim son chilhah hon gam alouva achenphana mun’u chu Bethel khopi le agamsunga kholen dom jouse toh, niso lama Naaran ahin, nilhum lama Gezer le akholen dung jouse jong ahithan, chule Shechem khopi le akholen len ho jong ahin, Ayyah khopi le akholen dung jouse changei jong ahithai.
English: Their possessions and settlements were Bethel and its towns, and eastward Naaran, and westward Gezer with its towns; Shechem also and its towns, to Azzah and its towns;

1CH 8:12
Thadou: Elpaal chapate chu Eber ahin, Misham ahin, chule Shemed ahi: ( Shemed hin Ono khopi le Lod khopi toh chule akholen dung jouse anasan ahin),
English: The sons of Elpaal: Eber, Misham, and Shemed, who built Ono and Lod, with its towns;

1CH 8:13
Thadou: Beriah ahin, chule Shema jong ahilhone. Amaho hi Aijalon khopi’a cheng insung phung upa cheh ahiuvin, chule Gath’a cheng ho toh kisat’a nomanga pang ho chu ahiuve.
English: and Beriah and Shema, who were heads of fathers’ households of the inhabitants of Aijalon, who put to flight the inhabitants of Gath;

1CH 9:7
Thadou: Benjamin phung kon’in Meshullam chapa Sallu ahin, Sallu chapa Hodaviah ahin, Hodaviah chapa Hassenuah ahin,
English: Of the sons of Benjamin: Sallu the son of Meshullam, the son of Hodaviah, the son of Hassenuah;

1CH 9:8
Thadou: Jeroham chapa Ibneiah ahin, chule Elah chu Uzzi chapa Micri chapa ahin, chule Meshullam jong chu Shephatiah chapa ahin, Shephatiah chu Reuel chapa ahin, Reuel chu Ibnijah chapa ahi.
English: and Ibneiah the son of Jeroham, and Elah the son of Uzzi, the son of Michri; and Meshullam the son of Shephatiah, the son of Reuel, the son of Ibnijah;

1CH 9:11
Thadou: Azariah kitipa Hilkiah chapa jong chu ahin, Hilkiah chu Meshullam chapa ahi; Meshullam chu Zadok chapa ahin, Zadok chu Meraioth chapa ahi; Meraioth chu Ahitub chapa ahi. Azariah chu Pathen hou-in’a vaibol lamkai pipua pang ahiye.
English: and Azariah the son of Hilkiah, the son of Meshullam, the son of Zadok, the son of Meraioth, the son of Ahitub, the ruler of God’s house;

1CH 9:12
Thadou: Thempu adang hung kinungle ho chu Jehoram chapa Adaiah ahin, Jehoram hi Pashhur chapa ahin, Pashhur chu Malkijah chapa ahin, chule Aiel chapa Maasai ahin, Meshullam chu Meshillemith chapa ahin, chule Meshillemith chu Immer chapa ahi.
English: and Adaiah the son of Jeroham, the son of Pashhur, the son of Malchijah; and Maasai the son of Adiel, the son of Jahzerah, the son of Meshullam, the son of Meshillemith, the son of Immer;

1CH 9:14
Thadou: Levi phunga mite chu Hasshub chapa Shemaiah ahin, Hasshub chu Azrikam chapa ahi; Hazrikam chu Hashabiah chapa ahin, Hashabiah chu Merari chapate lah’a khat ahi.
English: Of the Levites: Shemaiah the son of Hasshub, the son of Azrikam, the son of Hashabiah, of the sons of Merari;

1CH 11:33
Thadou: Baha'rum khoa mi Az'maveth jong ahin, Sha'al'bon kho a mi Eli'ahba jong ahi;
English: Azmaveth the Baharumite, Eliahba the Shaalbonite,

1CH 11:35
Thadou: Harar khoa mi mama Sachar chapa Ahi'am ahin, Ur chapa Eli'phal jong ahi;
English: Ahiam the son of Sacar the Hararite, Eliphal the son of Ur,

1CH 11:40
Thadou: Ithir kho kon Ira ahin, Ithir kho a mi ma ma Gareb ahi;
English: Ira the Ithrite, Gareb the Ithrite,

1CH 12:3
Thadou: Gabiah mi Shemah chapa Ahiezar hi amaho dia lamkai pipu pen ahin amanoi bantah a lamkai chu Joash ahi. Chule Azmaoth chapateni Pelet le Jeziel, Bareah le Anathoth kho a kon Jehu jong ahi.
English: The chief was Ahiezer, then Joash, the sons of Shemaah the Gibeathite; Jeziel and Pelet, the sons of Azmaveth; Beracah; Jehu the Anathothite;

1CH 12:4
Thadou: Gebeon a kon Ishmiah kitipa hi galhang somthum ho lah a lamkai le kinthang pen ahi. Chule Gederah kho a kon Jerrmiah, Jahaziel, Johanan le Jozabad ahiuve.
English: Ishmaiah the Gibeonite, a mighty man among the thirty and a leader of the thirty; Jeremiah; Jahaziel; Johanan; Jozabad the Gederathite;

1CH 12:5
Thadou: Haruph kho a kon Eluzai, Jeremoth, Beliah, Shemariah le Sephatiah ahiuve.
English: Eluzai; Jerimoth; Bealiah; Shemariah; Shephatiah the Haruphite;

1CH 12:6
Thadou: Korahites phung a kon Elkanah , Issiah, Azarel, Joezor le Jashobeam ahi.
English: Elkanah, Isshiah, Azarel, Joezer, and Jashobeam, the Korahites;

1CH 15:5
Thadou: Uriel lamkai na akon in Kohath nambah ami jakhat le somni ahin ,
English: of the sons of Kohath, Uriel the chief, and his brothers one hundred twenty;

1CH 15:6
Thadou: Asaiah lamkai na a Meraei nambah akon mi janile somni ahi,
English: of the sons of Merari, Asaiah the chief, and his brothers two hundred twenty;

1CH 15:7
Thadou: Joel lamkai na akon Gerahon nambah mi jale somthum alhing uve,
English: of the sons of Gershom, Joel the chief, and his brothers one hundred thirty;

1CH 15:8
Thadou: Elizaphan son chilhah akon Shemaiah lamkaina mi jani alhing e,
English: of the sons of Elizaphan, Shemaiah the chief, and his brothers two hundred;

1CH 15:9
Thadou: Hebron son chilhah a kon Eliel lamkai na in mi somget alhing uve,
English: of the sons of Hebron, Eliel the chief, and his brothers eighty;

1CH 15:17
Thadou: Chuin Levi hon jong Joel chapa Heman Levi tetoh sopi Merari nambah sung a kon Berekiah chapa ahin, Kushaiah chapa Ethan ho cheng ana pan sah uvin ahi.
English: So the Levites appointed Heman the son of Joel; and of his brothers, Asaph the son of Berechiah; and of the sons of Merari their brothers, Ethan the son of Kushaiah;

1CH 15:19
Thadou: Tumging them lah a Heman , Asaph le Ethan ho chu sumeng semjang sai ding in ana lheng uvin,
English: So the singers, Heman, Asaph, and Ethan, were given cymbals of bronze to sound aloud;

1CH 15:20
Thadou: Chule Zechariah, Aziel, Shemiramoth, Jehiel, Unni, Eliab, Measaiah le Benaiah ho cheng chu selang dah sai din ana lheng doh uvin ahi.
English: and Zechariah, Aziel, Shemiramoth, Jehiel, Unni, Eliab, Maaseiah, and Benaiah, with stringed instruments set to Alamoth;

1CH 16:5
Thadou: Asaph chu amaho lah a lamkai ahin, amahin lasah na a kimang tumging sumeng kivo ging asai yin ahi. Amaban tah’a chu Zechariah ahin chule ama kithopi ding in Jeiel, Mattithiah, Eliab, Benaiah, Obed-edom le Jeiel ahiuve. Amaho hi semjang le selangdah sai a pang ahiuve.
English: Asaph the chief, and second to him Zechariah, then Jeiel, Shemiramoth, Jehiel, Mattithiah, Eliab, Benaiah, Obed-Edom, and Jeiel, with stringed instruments and with harps; and Asaph with cymbals, sounding aloud;

1CH 16:37
Thadou: Hitichun David in Pakai kitepna thingkong a aniseh a angaichat najouse a natong le ding in Asaph le ama mi Levi mite chu ana pansah in ahi.
English: So he left Asaph and his brothers there before the ark of the LORD’s covenant, to minister before the ark continually, as every day’s work required;

1CH 16:38
Thadou: Hiche holah a chun Jeduthun chapa Obed-edom, Hosah le Levi mite misom gup le get chu kotkhah ngah in ana pang uve.
English: and Obed-Edom with their sixty-eight relatives; Obed-Edom also the son of Jeduthun and Hosah to be doorkeepers;

1CH 16:40
Thadou: Pakai in Israel te chung a dan thupeh juidia ana nei bang in amahon Pakai a jingkah nilhah in kilhaina thilpeh maicham jong ana nei uve,
English: to offer burnt offerings to the LORD on the altar of burnt offering continually morning and evening, even according to all that is written in the LORD’s law, which he commanded to Israel;

1CH 16:41
Thadou: Pakai akitah nale mingailut na tonsot na athoh hat na jallin ama thang vah na pe ding in David in Heman le Jeduthun ana lhengdoh un chule midang ana minphah chan jong ana pang uvin ahi.
English: and with them Heman and Jeduthun and the rest who were chosen, who were mentioned by name, to give thanks to the LORD, because his loving kindness endures forever;

1CH 17:4
Thadou: “Chenlang kasohpa David kom a gahiltan nangma hi keima umna ding munsem ding chu nahipoi’tin ana sei e.”
English: “Go and tell David my servant, ‘The LORD says, “You shall not build me a house to dwell in;

1CH 17:13
Thadou: Hiche mipa ding a chu keima hi apa kahi a ama chu kachapa hiding ahi. Nangma masang a mipa chung a kangailutna kana lahdoh bang a, ama chung a hi kanung lah doh lou ding ahi.
English: I will be his father, and he will be my son. I will not take my loving kindness away from him, as I took it from him who was before you;

1CH 18:15
Thadou: Zeruiah chapa Joab chu sepai lamkai in apang in chule Ahilud chapa Jehosaphet chu thuching le lekha sun in ana pang in ahi.
English: Joab the son of Zeruiah was over the army; Jehoshaphat the son of Ahilud was recorder;

1CH 18:16
Thadou: Ahitub chapa Zadok le Abiathar chapa Ahimeleche chu thempun apang lhon in chule Seraiah kitipa chu thutanna mun a lekha sun in apang e.
English: Zadok the son of Ahitub and Abimelech the son of Abiathar were priests; Shavsha was scribe;

1CH 22:15
Thadou: Natong ding mihem tampi semdoh in: song kheng them miho, thing thembol miho, thing vaibol miho, aloi loija mihem simjou lou mihem khutthemna neiho nakoi ding, khut themna neitah beh,
English: There are also workmen with you in abundance—cutters and workers of stone and timber, and all kinds of men who are skillful in every kind of work;

1CH 23:28
Thadou: Levi techun Pathen houbuh a Aaron chapate akithopiuva, indan ho sutheng le ding, thil thengho koitup ding chule Pathen houbuh a natoh chengse vetup ding ahiuve.
English: For their duty was to wait on the sons of Aaron for the service of the LORD’s house—in the courts, in the rooms, and in the purifying of all holy things, even the work of the service of God’s house;

1CH 23:29
Thadou: Dokhanga changlhah luidoh ding, todoh ding changbong ho chule ajat alet aneo dungjui a haltoh ding chengse jong avettup diu ahi.
English: for the show bread also, and for the fine flour for a meal offering, whether of unleavened wafers, or of that which is baked in the pan, or of that which is soaked, and for all measurements of quantity and size;

1CH 23:30
Thadou: Jingkah seh le ding uva Pathena vahchoi dingu ahi. Nilhah le angaima banga abol kit diu ahi.
English: and to stand every morning to thank and praise the LORD, and likewise in the evening;

1CH 23:31
Thadou: Chule amahon Sabbath nikho le Lhathah nikho a Pakai anga thilto abol teng ule amijat ana ngaichat dungjui a abol diu ahi.
English: and to offer all burnt offerings to the LORD on the Sabbaths, on the new moons, and on the set feasts, in number according to the ordinance concerning them, continually before the LORD;

1CH 25:9
Thadou: Mi jani somget le get ho hin, chapa somle ni cheh in asauvin, hichengse ho hi hop somni le li in aki homson uvin asopite cheng to vang akisan uve.Vang kisan masapen chu Asaph chilhah lah a Joseph le asopite ahiuvin. Anina a vang kisan chu Gedaliah le asopite ahi,
English: Now the first lot came out for Asaph to Joseph; the second to Gedaliah, he and his brothers and sons were twelve;

1CH 25:24
Thadou: a somle sagi na Joshbekashah,
English: for the seventeenth to Joshbekashah, his sons and his brothers, twelve;

1CH 25:30
Thadou: a somni le thumna Mahazioth,
English: for the twenty-third to Mahazioth, his sons and his brothers, twelve;

1CH 27:16
Thadou: Reuben phung lamkai chu Zicri, Eliezer chapa ahi. Simeon phung lamkai chu Maacah chapa, Shephatiah ahi.
English: Furthermore over the tribes of Israel: of the Reubenites, Eliezer the son of Zichri was the ruler; of the Simeonites, Shephatiah the son of Maacah;

1CH 27:17
Thadou: Levi Phung lamkai, Kemuel chapa Hashabiah ahin, Aaron themgaote phung lamkai chu Zadok ahi.
English: of Levi, Hashabiah the son of Kemuel; of Aaron, Zadok;

1CH 27:18
Thadou: Judah te lamkai chu David sopipa Elihu ahin, Issachar lamkai chu Michael chapa Omri ahi.
English: of Judah, Elihu, one of the brothers of David; of Issachar, Omri the son of Michael;

1CH 27:19
Thadou: Zebulun lamkai in Obadiah chapa Ishmaiah apangin, Naphtali lamkai chu Azriel chapa Jeremoth ahi.
English: of Zebulun, Ishmaiah the son of Obadiah; of Naphtali, Jeremoth the son of Azriel;

1CH 27:20
Thadou: Ephraim Phung lamkai chu Azaziah chapa Hoshea ahin, Lhumlam Manasseh lamkai chu Pedaiah chapa Joel ahi.
English: of the children of Ephraim, Hoshea the son of Azaziah; of the half-tribe of Manasseh, Joel the son of Pedaiah;

1CH 27:21
Thadou: Solam Gilead a Manasseh lamkai chu Zechariah chapa Iddo ahi. Benjamin lamkai a Abner chapa Jaasiel apang in.
English: of the half-tribe of Manasseh in Gilead, Iddo the son of Zechariah; of Benjamin, Jaasiel the son of Abner;

1CH 27:25
Thadou: Adiel chapa Azmaveth chu lengpa thilkholna ngahtup din nganse ahin, Uzziah chapa Jonathan chu khopi thilkholna mun jouse ngahtup din nganse ahitai.
English: Over the king’s treasures was Azmaveth the son of Adiel. Over the treasures in the fields, in the cities, in the villages, and in the towers was Jonathan the son of Uzziah;

1CH 28:11
Thadou: Chuin, David in athilgon ejakai, thil kholna indan ho chule chonset kingaidam na munho umdol jouse Solomon apetan ahi.
English: Then David gave to Solomon his son the plans for the porch of the temple, for its houses, for its treasuries, for its upper rooms, for its inner rooms, for the place of the mercy seat;

1CH 28:12
Thadou: David in alunggil a agontohsa, Houin lim asung apo, indan dang dang chule Maicham kibolna Muntheng dia agon ho jouse achapa Solomon aseipeh tai.
English: and the plans of all that he had by the Spirit, for the courts of the LORD’s house, for all the surrounding rooms, for the treasuries of God’s house, and for the treasuries of the dedicated things;

1CH 28:14
Thadou: David in Pathen Hou na a Sana le Sum eng man dia lom jat jong ahiltoh in,
English: of gold by weight for the gold for all vessels of every kind of service, for all the vessels of silver by weight, for all vessels of every kind of service;

1CH 28:15
Thadou: Solomon jah a Sana thaomei semna ding le sum eng thaomei semna ding chuleh sana le sum eng alut ding jat jong ahilthem in ahi.
English: by weight also for the lamp stands of gold, and for its lamps, of gold, by weight for every lamp stand and for its lamps; and for the lamp stands of silver, by weight for every lamp stand and for its lamps, according to the use of every lamp stand;

1CH 28:16
Thadou: Changlhah hung kitohdoh ho koina ding Sana theng a kisem Dokhang chule, sum eng a kisem dokhang ho jong akisem na a sana angaicha ding jat jong ahilthem e.
English: and the gold by weight for the tables of show bread, for every table; and silver for the tables of silver;

1CH 28:17
Thadou: Thih-khe sana thengsel ijat a sem a, khon, Kong, Sil kong ho jouse sana ijat cheh a sem ding aboncha a atetoh peh soh e.
English: and the forks, the basins, and the cups, of pure gold; and for the golden bowls by weight for every bowl; and for the silver bowls by weight for every bowl;

1CH 29:4
Thadou: Chuleh, keiman Houin bang dung ho sah nadin, Ophir a kon Sana talent jakhat somleni chuleh, sum eng thengsel talent jani somgup le ni jong kapedoh tai.
English: even three thousand talents of gold, of the gold of Ophir, and seven thousand talents of refined silver, with which to overlay the walls of the houses;

1CH 29:6
Thadou: Hichun, mi upa ho le Israel phung lamkai ho ahin, sepai jalamkaiho, gouching ho chuleh, lengpa vaibolho jouse jong kiphaltheng tah in akipedohsoh taove.
English: Then the princes of the fathers’ households, and the princes of the tribes of Israel, and the captains of thousands and of hundreds, with the rulers over the king’s work, offered willingly;

1CH 29:18
Thadou: Vo thaneipen Pathen, Kapu’u Abraham Pathen, Isaac Pathen, Israelte Pathen, namiten nathu angai jing ding uvin kahung tao’e. Nangma na jabol le na hepi nao jong mu jing’in.
English: LORD, the God of Abraham, of Isaac, and of Israel, our fathers, keep this desire forever in the thoughts of the heart of your people, and prepare their heart for you;

2CH 2:3
Thadou: Solomon chun Tyre Lengpa Hiram henga dingin thu hiti hin athot in “Kapa David in a chenna ding leng inpi asahna dinga, Cedar thing nana bolpeh ji bangchun keima jong neihin bolpeh in;
English: Solomon sent to Huram the king of Tyre, saying, “As you dealt with David my father, and sent him cedars to build him a house in which to dwell, so deal with me.

2CH 2:15
Thadou: Hiti ahijeh chun tun Kapun naseisaho suhlou changbong, sakol chang, lengpithei twi le olive thao twi chu neihin thot jengtan,” ati.
English: “Now therefore, the wheat, the barley, the oil, and the wine which my lord has spoken of, let him send to his servants;

2CH 4:15
Thadou: Twipi kiti kongtong le anoija bongchal ho;
English: one sea, and the twelve oxen under it.

2CH 4:20
Thadou: Akisemdoh akisei banga muntheng chungnunga vahding, sana thengsella kisem sana thaomei le thaomei khom ho;
English: and the lamp stands with their lamps to burn according to the ordinance before the inner sanctuary, of pure gold;

2CH 4:21
Thadou: Pahcha kijemhoi ho, thaomei chule chaiche ho chu aboncha sana thengsella kisemcheh ahiuve.
English: and the flowers, the lamps, and the tongs of gold that was purest gold;

2CH 5:4
Thadou: Israel upa ho jouse ahunglhun phat uchun Levi techun thingkong chu adomdoh-un;
English: All the elders of Israel came. The Levites took up the ark.

2CH 5:11
Thadou: Chuin thempuho chun muntheng chu adalha tauve . Thempuho chu hiche nikho kin; kibolnaa panghen lang panghih jongle abon chaovin akisutheng soh keiyun ahi.
English: When the priests had come out of the holy place (for all the priests who were present had sanctified themselves, and didn’t keep their divisions;

2CH 5:12
Thadou: Chule Levite lasa themho Asaph, Heman Jeduthun chule asopiho le achateu chu tupat pon nemin akivon nun, maicham solama chun adingun; semjang pehkhong le selangdah atum un ahi. Amaho chu thempuho jakhat le somni chun sumkon mutnin akitho piuvin ahi.
English: also the Levites who were the singers, all of them, even Asaph, Heman, Jeduthun, and their sons and their brothers, arrayed in fine linen, with cymbals and stringed instruments and harps, stood at the east end of the altar, and with them one hundred twenty priests sounding with trumpets);

2CH 6:5
Thadou: “Kami Israelte Egypt gam'a kahin puidoh nikhoa pat chun, Kamin ki jana ding Houin sahna ding in; Israel phung sunga khopi dang kalhengpoi chule kami Israelte chunga vaihom ding in koima dang kalhengpoi.
English: ‘Since the day that I brought my people out of the land of Egypt, I chose no city out of all the tribes of Israel to build a house in, that my name might be there, and I chose no man to be prince over my people Israel;

2CH 6:8
Thadou: “Ahinlah Pakai chun kapa jah’a kamin jabolna ding Houin khat sahdinga nagel chu apha lheh’e atin ahi.
English: But the LORD said to David my father, ‘Whereas it was in your heart to build a house for my name, you did well that it was in your heart;

2CH 6:14
Thadou: Vo Pakai, Israel Pathen van le leiya nangma tobang Pathen dang aumpoi, nangman nakitepna nanit jing in, alungthim pumpia nangma kom hinjonna kipedohte nalungsetna longlou chu nachan jinge.
English: Then he said, “LORD, the God of Israel, there is no God like you in heaven or on earth—you who keep covenant and loving kindness with your servants who walk before you with all their heart;

2CH 6:20
Thadou: asun ajanin hiche Houin a namin kijabolna dinga naseina mun hi nahin vetjing thei’a, chule nalhachate le namiten hiche mun lam nga-a taona ahin man tengule nahin ngai na din;
English: that your eyes may be open toward this house day and night, even toward the place where you have said that you would put your name, to listen to the prayer which your servant will pray toward this place.

2CH 6:24
Thadou: Namite Israelte chun nangma dounaa achonset jeh uva, gal aleluva achonset nau akona ahung kiheikit uva; chule nangma angsunga ahung kineosah uva, nangma nahin koukituva ahungtao kit ule;
English: “If your people Israel are struck down before the enemy because they have sinned against you, and they turn again and confess your name, and pray and make supplication before you in this house,

2CH 6:34
Thadou: Namite chu galsat dinga nasol dohnauva kona chu nangman nadeilhen khopi lam ngatna, chule nangma min kijabolna dinga kasadoh Houin lam ngatna ahungtao teng ule,
English: “If your people go out to battle against their enemies, by whatever way you send them, and they pray to you toward this city which you have chosen, and the house which I have built for your name;

2CH 6:36
Thadou: Aitih’a chonse ngailou nangma dounaa achonset tengule, nangman amaho chunga nalung hanna; chutengle amaho chu agalmiten jou uvintin, gampam mi anai hijongle agamla hijongle sohchangin kaimang tauhen.
English: “If they sin against you (for there is no man who doesn’t sin), and you are angry with them and deliver them to the enemy, so that they carry them away captive to a land far off or near;

2CH 6:38
Thadou: asoh channau gamma chu alungthim pumpiu le alhagao pumpia ahung kinung heikit uva, apu apateu nana pehsa gam lam ngatna chule nangman nalhentum khopi lam ahin ngat uva, namin jabolna'a kisadoh Houin lam nga-a ahungtao tengule,
English: if they return to you with all their heart and with all their soul in the land of their captivity, where they have been taken captive, and pray toward their land which you gave to their fathers, and the city which you have chosen, and toward the house which I have built for your name;

2CH 8:5
Thadou: Chunglam Beth-Horon le noilam Beth-Horon khopi ho chu kulpi akai in, abang ho athah sah kitnin chule thihkot aton ahi.
English: Also he built Beth Horon the upper and Beth Horon the lower, fortified cities with walls, gates, and bars;

2CH 15:12
Thadou: Chuin amaho alung thim pumpi alhagao pumpiu vin Pakai a-Pathen’u holnan kitepna khat asemdoh tauvin ahi.
English: They entered into the covenant to seek the LORD, the God of their fathers, with all their heart and with all their soul;

2CH 17:7
Thadou: Jehosophat Leng chan kal kum thum lhin kum chun, Judah khopi jousea amilen amilal ho chu mihil dingin asollin ahi. Hiche Milen milal ho chu Benhiel, Obadiah, Zechariah, Nathaniel chule Micaiah ahiuve. Elishana le Jeroboam thempu teni jong asoldoh in ahi.
English: Also in the third year of his reign he sent his princes, even Ben Hail, Obadiah, Zechariah, Nethanel, and Micaiah, to teach in the cities of Judah;

2CH 17:14
Thadou: Judah phunga konin sepai sang jathum, honkhatna sangkhat cheh chu Adnah lamkaina noija aum uvin ahi.
English: This was the numbering of them according to their fathers’ houses: From Judah, the captains of thousands: Adnah the captain, and with him three hundred thousand mighty men of valor;

2CH 17:15
Thadou: Ama noichetna lamkai chu Jehohanan ahin, aman sepai sang jani le sang somget alamkai in ahi.
English: and next to him Jehohanan the captain, and with him two hundred eighty thousand;

2CH 17:17
Thadou: Benjamin phunga konin thalpi le pho mangcha sepai sang jani aumme, amaho chu sepai tamtah Eleada lamkai na noiya um ahiuve.
English: From Benjamin: Eliada, a mighty man of valor, and with him two hundred thousand armed with bow and shield;

2CH 18:25
Thadou: Hichun Israel lengpan a sepai lamkai komma chun, man inlang khopi vaihompa leh leng chapa Joash kommah ga pelut tan ati.
English: The king of Israel said, “Take Micaiah, and carry him back to Amon the governor of the city, and to Joash the king’s son;

2CH 20:5
Thadou: Hitichun Jerusalem ma Judah mipite jousechu Pakai houinsung indan thah kisem maija chun akikhom mun, Jehoshaphat lengpa jong achen amasang uvah adingin ahi
English: Jehoshaphat stood in the assembly of Judah and Jerusalem, in the LORD’s house, before the new court;

2CH 20:10
Thadou: Chuleh tuhin Ammon mite, Moab mite, chuleh molchunga um Seir mite aummun ahi, amahohi Egyptma konna Israel tea hung dohuva chu amato kisatding neina phalpeh lou ahi hijeha chu amahochu sumang louva ana otdohu ahi.
English: Now, behold, the children of Ammon and Moab and Mount Seir, whom you would not let Israel invade when they came out of the land of Egypt, but they turned away from them, and didn’t destroy them;

2CH 20:14
Thadou: Hichun Pakai lhagao chu khoppilah achun Asaph chatelaha konna Levi mipa Mattaniah chapa, Jeiel chapa Benaiah chapa Zechariah chapa Jahaziel chunga Pakai lhagao ahung chun,
English: Then the LORD’s Spirit came on Jahaziel the son of Zechariah, the son of Benaiah, the son of Jeiel, the son of Mattaniah, the Levite, of the sons of Asaph, in the middle of the assembly;

2CH 21:14
Thadou: Hichejeha hi Pakaiyin na mipite leh nacha nanao teleh najite asuhgenthei ding chuleh naneinagou hojong asuhmang ding ahi
English: behold, the LORD will strike your people with a great plague, including your children, your wives, and all your possessions;

2CH 21:16
Thadou: Hiche chung chon hin Pakaiyin Philistine teleh Ethopia komma cheng Arabiate Jehoram doudingin ahin choudoh tan ahi
English: The LORD stirred up against Jehoram the spirit of the Philistines and of the Arabians who are beside the Ethiopians;

2CH 29:12
Thadou: Hichun Levi te ahung kipatdoh taove: Amasai chapa Mahath chuleh Azariah chapa Joel, Kohathites chateho Merari chateho, Abdi chapa Kish chuleh Jehallelel chapa Azariah, Gershon chateho Zimmah chapa Joash chuleh Joash chapa Eden
English: Then the Levites arose: Mahath, the son of Amasai, and Joel the son of Azariah, of the sons of the Kohathites; and of the sons of Merari, Kish the son of Abdi, and Azariah the son of Jehallelel; and of the Gershonites, Joah the son of Zimmah, and Eden the son of Joah;

2CH 29:13
Thadou: Elizaphan chate chu Shimri leh Jeiel ahin, Asaph chate chu Zechariah leh Mattaniah ahin,
English: and of the sons of Elizaphan, Shimri and Jeuel; and of the sons of Asaph, Zechariah and Mattaniah;

2CH 31:15
Thadou: Thempuho chenna khopi dung ho a chun, ama chu Levi mi hicheng hin ana kithopiovin ahi; Eden, Miniamin, Jeshua, Shemiah, Amariah leh Shecaniah ahiove. Amaho hin asopio Levi hochu anatoh u dungjui cheh in kibang cheh in anahom doh jiovin ahi
English: Under him were Eden, Miniamin, Jeshua, Shemaiah, Amariah, and Shecaniah, in the cities of the priests, in their office of trust, to give to their brothers by divisions, to the great as well as to the small;

2CH 31:16
Thadou: Phung le chang dungjuija hilouvin, amahon pasal ho chu kum 30 lhingle achunga hochu houinna amoppoh nao apanmunnu dungjuijin achandiu ahoppeh un ahi
English: in addition to those who were listed by genealogy of males, from three years old and upward, even everyone who entered into the LORD’s house, as the duty of every day required, for their service in their offices according to their divisions;

2CH 31:17
Thadou: Thempu hochun aphung dung juiyin tohding apeovin chuleh Levi hochu kum 20 lhingleh atahjo hochu anatoh dungjuijin nganse na aneiyun ahi
English: and those who were listed by genealogy of the priests by their fathers’ houses, and the Levites from twenty years old and upward, in their offices by their divisions;

2CH 32:27
Thadou: Hezekiah chun neilegou ahaolheh jengtaan jana lentah jong achangin ahi. Aman sana le dangka chuleh song mantam, namtwi ho, ompho holeh thilman tamtah ho koinading dankhat jong asaovin ahi
English: Hezekiah had exceedingly great riches and honor. He provided himself with treasuries for silver, for gold, for precious stones, for spices, for shields, and for all kinds of valuable vessels;

2CH 36:15
Thadou: Apu apateo Pakaiyin ama ho gihsal dingin a themgao hou ahin soljingin ahi. Ajeh chu aman amite a houin chu athenga aumding akhohsah ahi
English: The LORD, the God of their fathers, sent to them by his messengers, rising up early and sending, because he had compassion on his people and on his dwelling place;

EZR 1:7
Thadou: Lengpa Nebuchadnezzar in Jerusalem houin na anakoi khontheng hojong chu Cyrus lengpan amaho pathen houin a kon in ahin ladohtan ahi.
English: Also Cyrus the king brought out the vessels of the LORD’s house, which Nebuchadnezzar had brought out of Jerusalem, and had put in the house of his gods;

EZR 2:1
Thadou: Mihem hijatpi hi gamsung mi sohchanna a konna hung kinungle kit ho chu ahiuvin, amahohi Babylon lengpa Nebuchadnezzar kitipan sohchang dinga anakai mangho chu ahiuve, abonchauvin amahohi Judah gamsunga Jerusalem khopi lamma ahung kile uvin ama ama khosung cheh a akile kit taovin ahi.
English: Now these are the children of the province who went up out of the captivity of those who had been carried away, whom Nebuchadnezzar the king of Babylon had carried away to Babylon, and who returned to Jerusalem and Judah, everyone to his city;

EZR 2:2
Thadou: Miho chu Zeubbabel leh Jeshua, Nehemiah, Seraiah, Reelaiah, Mordecai, Bilshan, Mispar, Bigvai, Rehum chule Ba’anah lamkai nan ahung kitol uvin ahi. Israel mite amijat mong mong chu;
English: who came with Zerubbabel, Jeshua, Nehemiah, Seraiah, Reelaiah, Mordecai, Bilshan, Mispar, Bigvai, Rehum, and Baanah. The number of the men of the people of Israel:

EZR 2:64
Thadou: Sohchang a hungkile mihem pumpi chu abonchauvin mihem sangsom li le sangni toh, ja thumle som gup alhing uvin ahi;
English: The whole assembly together was forty-two thousand three hundred sixty,

EZR 2:66
Thadou: Amahon sakol jasagi le somthum le gup, asakolpol jong ja ni le som li le nga;
English: Their horses were seven hundred thirty-six; their mules, two hundred forty-five;

EZR 3:4
Thadou: Amahon Lhambuh Kut abollun, hichu Mose daan dungjuija niseh le anikho a ngaichat dolla pumgo thiltoa kilhaina ding jongchu atoh jengun ahi.
English: They kept the feast of booths, as it is written, and offered the daily burnt offerings by number, according to the ordinance, as the duty of every day required;

EZR 6:3
Thadou: “Cyrus lengpa vaihom kumkhat channa in lengpan thu anapen Jerusalem’a houin chu kilhaina gantha kibol naleh pumgo thilto kitonaji houin chu kithah sahkit hen, a-in sandol chu tong somgup hihenlang availam jong tong somgup ma hihen.
English: In the first year of Cyrus the king, Cyrus the king made a decree: Concerning God’s house at Jerusalem, let the house be built, the place where they offer sacrifices, and let its foundations be strongly laid, with its height sixty cubits and its width sixty cubits;

EZR 7:27
Thadou: Hichun Ezra in jong, “Ipu ipateo Pathen chu thangvah in umhen ajeh chu aman lengpa amangchan Jerusalem’a Pakai houin asemhoi tan ahi!
English: Blessed be the LORD, the God of our fathers, who has put such a thing as this in the king’s heart, to beautify the LORD’s house which is in Jerusalem;

EZR 8:18
Thadou: Ka Pathen u khotona khut chun eipuihoi jeh un, amahon Sherebiah kitipa achate le asopite somle get eihin solpeh un ahi. Amachu Israel chapa Levi chilhah ho lah a Mahli chilhah minasatah khat ahi.
English: According to the good hand of our God on us they brought us a man of discretion, of the sons of Mahli, the son of Levi, the son of Israel, namely Sherebiah, with his sons and his brothers, eighteen;

EZR 8:19
Thadou: Amahon Merari chilhah holah a kon’in Hashabiah chule Jeshaiah toh ahinsol thauvin chuleh achate le asopite somni jong ahin sollun chuleh
English: and Hashabiah, and with him Jeshaiah of the sons of Merari, his brothers and their sons, twenty;

EZR 9:5
Thadou: Kilhaina phat ahung lhunphat in von kibottel pumleh lungkham puma katouna a konin kahung dingdoh jengin, kadilsun ka Pathen langa chun kakhut kadom sangin,
English: At the evening offering I rose up from my humiliation, even with my garment and my robe torn; and I fell on my knees, and spread out my hands to the LORD my God;

EZR 10:7
Thadou: Hichejou chun Judah leh Jerusalem gam pumpi sungah thuphon khat aphongdoh un sohchang hung kilekit jouse Jerusalem’a hung kikhom dingin thupeh anei taovin ahi.
English: They made a proclamation throughout Judah and Jerusalem to all the children of the captivity, that they should gather themselves together to Jerusalem;

NEH 1:8
Thadou: Chule nangman nalhachapa Mose koma nanaseisa, “Nangho keima koma nakitah lou’ule keiman chitin namtin laha kathe cheh ding nahiuve.
English: “Remember, I beg you, the word that you commanded your servant Moses, saying, ‘If you trespass, I will scatter you among the peoples;

NEH 2:4
Thadou: Hichun lengpan eidongin’ “Aphai; chuti chu ahileh ipi lampen a kaki thopi thei ding ham?” eiti; hichun keima van Pathen koma kataovin;
English: Then the king said to me, “What is your request?” So I prayed to the God of heaven.

NEH 2:7
Thadou: Lengpa koma chun keiman kaseibe kitin, “Lengpa nalung alhai dinga ahile, Eupharates vadung gal lhanglam gamkaiya gam vaipo ho koma lekha eijih peh in lang Judah gam kajot na a agamsungu boilouhel a kajot galkai theina dingin thupeh neithot peh in,” kati.
English: Moreover I said to the king, “If it pleases the king, let letters be given me to the governors beyond the River, that they may let me pass through until I come to Judah;

NEH 3:25
Thadou: Uzai chapa Palal chun agal langkhat in ningkoi lai chule insang laitah toh kigalsai lai, chule lengpa indan chung nung, in vengtup ho panna indan laitah chu asemphan ahi; chule ama bantah a hin Parosh chapa Pedai’ah leh;
English: Palal the son of Uzai made repairs opposite the turning of the wall, and the tower that stands out from the upper house of the king, which is by the court of the guard. After him Pedaiah the son of Parosh made repairs.

NEH 4:7
Thadou: Ahinla hitobang tah a hi natoh achal a Jerusalem pal achimsa lai jouse akisemphat hi Sanballat le Tobiah chuleh Arab mite, Amon mite le Ashdod miten ajahdoh phat’un alunghang lheh jeng tauvin ahi.
English: But when Sanballat, Tobiah, the Arabians, the Ammonites, and the Ashdodites heard that the repairing of the walls of Jerusalem went forward, and that the breaches began to be filled, they were very angry;

NEH 6:1
Thadou: Kamelmateu Sanballat, Tobiah, Geshem kiti Arab mipale midang hon, kotpi chengse le kelkot dunga katundoh loulai vangun, Jerusalem pal chu akigen chaiyin avanglai mun khatcha aum tapoi ti amudoh phat’un;
English: Now when it was reported to Sanballat, Tobiah, Geshem the Arabian, and to the rest of our enemies that I had built the wall, and that there was no breach left in it (though even to that time I had not set up the doors in the gates),

NEH 7:68
Thadou: Asakol chengseu chu jasagi le somthum le gup ahin chule sakol pol chengse jong chu jani le somli le nga ahi.
English: Their horses were seven hundred thirty-six; their mules, two hundred forty-five;

NEH 8:14
Thadou: Dan chu akholchilbe phat’un Pathenin Mose mangcha a athupeh dungjuiya hiche lhasunga kut kibol sunga chu Israel lhambuh sunga umdiu ahi ti amudoh un ahi.
English: They found written in the law how the LORD had commanded by Moses that the children of Israel should dwell in booths in the feast of the seventh month;

