English: and perseverance, proven character; and proven character, hope;

ROM 6:5
Thadou: Ama thina a thikhom'ah ihiu banga chu, Ama thokit banga eiho jong hinna'a kaithouva umkit ding ihiu ahi.
English: For if we have become united with him in the likeness of his death, we will also be part of his resurrection;

ROM 7:9
Thadou: Phat khat'in Danthu hetna neilouvin kana hingin, hinla keiman, thupeh in, vetsahnan, neipap kiloset lou ding tia eihil kahetdoh chun, chonset thaneina chu kachungah ahung lhunge;
English: I was alive apart from the law once, but when the commandment came, sin revived and I died.

ROM 7:10
Thadou: chuleh keima athia kahitai. Hitichun, keiman Danthupeh hochun hinna ahinlhut ding doltah hinlhut talouvin Lhagao thina joh ahinlhut taiti kamudoh e.
English: The commandment which was for life, this I found to be for death;

ROM 8:6
Thadou: Hijeh chun, nachonset nomnau lungthim chun na-thununuva ahileh thinaa napuilut ding'u ahi. Hinla, Lhagao Theng'in nalungthim'u athunun a ahileh, hinna le lungmonna hiding ahi.
English: For the mind of the flesh is death, but the mind of the Spirit is life and peace;

ROM 8:16
Thadou: Ajehchu Ama Lhagao le eiho lhagao akijopmat chun Pathen chate ihiu aphotchen ahitai.
English: The Spirit himself testifies with our spirit that we are children of God;

ROM 9:4
Thadou: Amaho Israel mite ahiuvin, Pathen cha-lamthu hina changah ahiuvin, Pathen in aloupina amaho heng alhut ahitai. Aman amaho to kitepna aneiya chule a-Danthu apehdoh ahiuve. Aman amaho chu ahoutheina dinguva michonpha a asem ahin, chule athutep kidangtah ahin pehdoh ahiye.
English: who are Israelites; whose is the adoption, the glory, the covenants, the giving of the law, the service, and the promises;

ROM 9:27
Thadou: Chule Israel chung chang thua Themgao Isaiah chun ahinsamdoh in, Israel mite chu twikhanglen panga neldi jat tam'in tam jongleh, amoh them bou sohcha ding ahi,” ati.
English: Isaiah cries concerning Israel, “If the number of the children of Israel are as the sand of the sea, it is the remnant who will be saved;

ROM 9:30
Thadou: Hicheho jouse hi ipi kiseina hintem? Chidang namdang te Pathen chondan juilou ahivangun, amaho chu Pathen lungtoh dia kisema ahitauve. Chule tahsan hin hiche hi ahin hitheisah ahi.
English: What shall we say then? That the Gentiles, who didn’t follow after righteousness, attained to righteousness, even the righteousness which is of faith;

ROM 10:6
Thadou: Hinlah tahsanjal'a Pathen themchan theina ding chun, “Nangman nalung thima koi vana gakal ding ham (Christa chu vana kona agapuilhah ding kiseina ahi).
English: But the righteousness which is of faith says this, “Don’t say in your heart, ‘Who will ascend into heaven?’ (that is, to bring Christ down);

ROM 11:20
Thadou: Ahinai, hijongleh geldoh in: chuche abahho akisuhboh nau ajehchu amahon Christa atahsan lou jeh-u ahi, chule nangman natahsan jeh-a naum ahi. Hijehchun, kichoisang hih in, ahin ipi sohthei ding ahi thua kichajon.
English: True; by their unbelief they were broken off, and you stand by your faith. Don’t be conceited, but fear;

ROM 12:6
Thadou: Alungsetna'a Pathen in thilpeh jatchom chom cheh eipeh-u ahin, hichu phatah a iboltheina dingu ahi. Hijeh a chu Pathen in gao thusei theina napeh a ahileh, Pathen in napeh tahsan nanei dungjuiyin seijin.
English: having gifts differing according to the grace that was given to us: if prophecy, let’s prophesy according to the proportion of our faith;

ROM 12:7
Thadou: Lhagao thilpeh nachan chu midang kithopina dinga ahileh, phatah in kithopinan bol'in. Nangma mihil'a napanleh, phatah in hil'in.
English: or service, let’s give ourselves to service; or he who teaches, to his teaching;

ROM 15:19
Thadou: Amaho melchihna le datmo kidangho chule Lhagaotheng thahatna chun alunguva nopna anei sah ahi. Hitia hi keiman Christa Kipana Thuphahi Jerusalema pat Illyricum lampi geiya kapehdoh soh ahitai.
English: in the power of signs and wonders, in the power of God’s Spirit; so that from Jerusalem and around as far as to Illyricum, I have fully preached the Good News of Christ;

1CO 1:24
Thadou: Hinlah Pathen in huhhing dinga akou ho dingin vang, Judah mi hihen chidang namdang hijong leh, Christa chu Pathen thahatna le Pathen chihna ahigel e.
English: but to those who are called, both Jews and Greeks, Christ is the power of God and the wisdom of God;

1CO 1:26
Thadou: Kasopi deitahteho geldohtemun, Pathen in nanakou pet'u chun hiche vannoi lamdol a aching'ah ahilouleh athaneiyah ahilouleh ahaovah naum pouve.
English: For you see your calling, brothers, that not many are wise according to the flesh, not many mighty, and not many noble;

1CO 5:9
Thadou: Masanga nakom uva dinga lekha kahinjih a chu nangho jon lungpua chonse nomjing ho toh kivop hih un tia kanasei peh nahiu ahitai.
English: I wrote to you in my letter to have no company with sexual sinners;

1CO 7:29
Thadou: Tun sopite ho, hiche hi kahinsei nome: Phat aumbe nalai hi achom behseh e. Hijeh hin, jinei pasal hon ajineiyu hi akisahboi nau pipen hisah dauhen.
English: But I say this, brothers: the time is short. From now on, both those who have wives may be as though they had none;

1CO 7:30
Thadou: Akap ho ahilouleh akipah ho ahilouleh thilcho ho chu akanao ahilouleh akipanau ahilouleh athil neiyuva kipum phumlut dauhen.
English: and those who weep, as though they didn’t weep; and those who rejoice, as though they didn’t rejoice; and those who buy, as though they didn’t possess;

1CO 7:32
Thadou: Keiman hiche hinkho gelkhohna a kona hi naon thol dingu kadei ahi. Jineilou pasal chun aphat le alunggel chu Pakai iti lunglhaiya, ana iti atoh ding angaito ahi.
English: But I desire to have you to be free from cares. He who is unmarried is concerned for the things of the Lord, how he may please the Lord;

1CO 9:20
Thadou: Keima Judah te toh kaum khom pet'in, Judah te chu Christa a kapuilut theina dingin, Judah te tobang'in danthu noiya hinkho kamangin ahi.
English: To the Jews I became as a Jew, that I might gain Jews; to those who are under the law, as under the law, that I might gain those who are under the law;

1CO 10:1
Thadou: Kasopiteho, nanghon masangpeh a gamthip a ipu ipateu anaumu thudol chu nasuhmil dingu kanompoi. Amaho jouse chu achunguva um meibolin apuiyun, chule abonchauvin Twipisan chu tolgolai jot in ajot jenguve.
English: Now I would not have you ignorant, brothers, that our fathers were all under the cloud, and all passed through the sea;

1CO 10:2
Thadou: Mose nungjui ahijaluvin meibol sunga le twipi sunga chun abonun baptize achangun ahi.
English: and were all baptized into Moses in the cloud and in the sea;

1CO 10:3
Thadou: Amaho jouse chun lhagao an thakhat chu anecheh uvin,
English: and all ate the same spiritual food;

1CO 10:32
Thadou: Judah mite hihen lang, ahilouleh chidang namdang ho hijongleh, ahilouleh Pathen houbung hijongleh lungthoisah hih un.
English: Give no occasion for stumbling, whether to Jews, to Greeks, or to the assembly of God;

1CO 11:8
Thadou: Ajeh iham itileh mimasa chu numeiya kona ahipon, hinla numei masa chu pasala kon ahi.
English: For man is not from woman, but woman from man;

1CO 13:5
Thadou: ahilouleh a-engsepoi. Ama dei bou angeh gunsetpoi. Lung himo pina aneipon, chule akibol phat louna ho aching denpoi.
English: doesn’t behave itself inappropriately, doesn’t seek its own way, is not provoked, takes no account of evil;

1CO 13:6
Thadou: Adih louva kibol akipapi pon, hinla thutah chun ajo tengleh akipahji.
English: doesn’t rejoice in unrighteousness, but rejoices with the truth;

1CO 13:9
Thadou: Tua ihetthei nau hi alhasamin chule akimpon ahi, chule Pathen Thusei dohna thilpeh geiya hi aboncha hijoulou kiphasam nalai ahije.
English: For we know in part and we prophesy in part;

2CO 2:6
Thadou: Nangho atamjo chengsen kilungkhat tah a ama douna a thu natan uva chu gimbolna ama dinga aphakhopset kipea ahi.
English: This punishment which was inflicted by the many is sufficient for such a one;

2CO 4:8
Thadou: Keiho hi hahsatna hon aningtin'ah eidel phauvin, hinla eiki tatgoi pouve. Kalungu akichiah jin, hinla kalung lhapai jeng pouve.
English: We are pressed on every side, yet not crushed; perplexed, yet not to despair;

2CO 4:9
Thadou: Keiho delkhumin kaum un, hinla Pathen in einungsun deh pouve. Keiho eikison op uvin, hinla eiki sumangpai pouve.
English: pursued, yet not forsaken; struck down, yet not destroyed;

2CO 5:6
Thadou: Hiti chun keiho hiche tahsa a kahinlai sung uva hi Pakai to in'a umkhom'a kahi pouve ti kahetnau hi kisonpi khopset theiya hetna nei kahiu ahi.
English: Therefore we are always confident and know that while we are at home in the body, we are absent from the Lord;

2CO 5:18
Thadou: Chule hicheho jouse hi Christa jal'a Ama koma eilepuikit'u ahitah jeh in Pathena kona thilpeh ahije. Chule Pathen in miho chu Amatoh kichamna dinga ngansena eipeh u ahi.
English: But all things are of God, who reconciled us to himself through Jesus Christ, and gave to us the ministry of reconciliation;

2CO 10:3
Thadou: Keiho mihem kahiuvin, ahivangin mihem galsat in gal kasat pouve.
English: For though we walk in the flesh, we don’t wage war according to the flesh;

2CO 11:26
Thadou: Keima lamsaotah tah kana kholjinin ahi. Keiman vadung hoa le gucha michomho lah a vangsetna katoh in ahi. Keiman kamite, Judah nam'a konle chidang namdang ho lah a konin vangsetna katoh in ahi. Atahsan kahi tia ahia atahbeh ahilou jeh uvin amahoa konin tosetna katoh in ahi.
English: I have been in travels often, perils of rivers, perils of robbers, perils from my countrymen, perils from the Gentiles, perils in the city, perils in the wilderness, perils in the sea, perils among false brothers;

EPH 2:7
Thadou: Hitia chu Pathen in ahung lhung ding khanghoa alungsetna atepibei haosatna chu avetsahna a chule ichung uva hepina chu eiho jouse dinga athilbol jouse chu Christa Yeshua a eimu sah u ahitai.
English: that in the ages to come he might show the exceeding riches of his grace in kindness toward us in Christ Jesus;

EPH 2:20
Thadou: Akigoma eiho hi Ama in chu ihiuvin, solchah ho le themgao ho bulphuna a chu kisadoh a ihiuve. Inninga songpia panga chu Christa Yeshua Ama tah ahi.
English: being built on the foundation of the apostles and prophets, Christ Jesus himself being the chief cornerstone;

EPH 2:21
Thadou: Eiho chingtheitah a Amato kijopmat a ihiuvin, Pakai dinga hou-in theng khat ihiuve.
English: in whom the whole building, fitted together, grows into a holy temple in the Lord;

EPH 4:11
Thadou: Tun hiche ho hi Christa in a houbung dinga manbei thilpeh'a apeh ahi: Solchah ho, Themgao ho, Evangelist ho, Pastor ho chule Mihil ho ahiuve.
English: He gave some to be apostles; and some, prophets; and some, evangelists; and some, shepherds and teachers;

EPH 4:14
Thadou: Chutengleh eiho chapang ho banga pilhing louva iumlou dingu ahitai. Eiho hi thuhil thah hui hung nung tobang ahung ho chun eimut lonle le lou dingu ahitai. Eiho hi mihon jouva eihin doha bol teng uleh thutah banga chingtheitah a asei dingu ahi.
English: that we may no longer be children, tossed back and forth and carried about with every wind of doctrine, by the trickery of men, in craftiness, after the wiles of error;

EPH 5:3
Thadou: Nalah uva jon-thanhoina, thenlouna, ahilouleh chipset umdahen. Hitobang chonsetnaho hin Pathen mite lah a mun aneipoi.
English: But sexual immorality, and all uncleanness or covetousness, let it not even be mentioned among you, as becomes saints;

EPH 5:19
Thadou: Vahchoina la ho le Pathen houna la chule lhagaolam laho nangma ho lah a sauvin, chule nalunggilun Pakaiya tumging tothon sauvin.
English: speaking to one another in psalms, hymns, and spiritual songs; singing and making melody in your heart to the Lord;

EPH 5:20
Thadou: Chule imalam jousea Pa Pathen chu IPakaiyu Yeshua Christa minin thangvah un.
English: giving thanks always concerning all things in the name of our Lord Jesus Christ to God, even the Father;

EPH 6:17
Thadou: Huhhingna chu lukhuh in neiyun, chule Lhagao chemjam Pathen Thu chu panun.
English: And take the helmet of salvation, and the sword of the Spirit, which is the word of God;

PHP 1:5
Thadou: Ajehchu Christa Kipana Thupha hillhangna thudol a, najah masat niuva pat tuni changeiyin nangho katohkhompi nahi jing uve.
English: for your partnership in furtherance of the Good News from the first day until now;

PHP 1:16
Thadou: Amaho chun Kipana Thupha hongbit a panga kahi aheuvin, keima eingailut jeh uva aseiphongu ahi.
English: The former insincerely preach Christ from selfish ambition, thinking that they add affliction to my chains;

PHP 1:27
Thadou: Chukalvalin, nangho van-gam mite chonin chon un, Christa Kipana Thupha to kitoh in hinkho manguvin. Chuti chun keiman kahunga nangho kahungmu u hihen ahilouleh athua nachung thu'u kajah tho hijongleh, nangho lhagao khat le lungkhatpua nadin khomuva chule Kipana Thupha thua tahsan gal nasatu thudol chu henange.
English: Only let your way of life be worthy of the Good News of Christ, that whether I come and see you or am absent, I may hear of your state, that you stand firm in one spirit, with one soul striving for the faith of the Good News;

PHP 2:2
Thadou: Chuti ahileh nanghon neikipasah tahbeh uvin, chuti chun lung pumpia thukhat kisauvin, khat in khat ngailu uvin, chule lunggel kithakhat neiyin chule doi kithakhat hiuvin.
English: make my joy full by being like-minded, having the same love, being of one accord, of one mind;

PHP 2:3
Thadou: Chang kilunggel bol hih in, midang pachat hol hih'in. Kineosah in, nangma sanga midang chu aphajon gelin.
English: doing nothing through rivalry or through conceit, but in humility, each counting others better than himself;

PHP 3:3
Thadou: Ajeh iham itileh eiho Pathen lhagaova kon a Pathen hou cheptan tahbeh ihiuvin, Yeshua Christa natoh chaisa a chu kingamdet'a, tahsalama kisonna neilou ihiuve.
English: For we are the circumcision, who worship God in the Spirit, and rejoice in Christ Jesus, and have no confidence in the flesh;

PHP 3:5
Thadou: Keima ni-get nia cheptan kahin, Israel mi hina pen-gui chu kaneiyin, chule Benjamin phunga kon Hebrew mi atahbeh chu kahi. Judate Dan juina lama hakattah Pharisee ho lah a mi kahi;
English: circumcised the eighth day, of the stock of Israel, of the tribe of Benjamin, a Hebrew of Hebrews; concerning the law, a Pharisee;

COL 1:28
Thadou: Hijeh a hi keihon midang Christa thu kaseipeh uva, amitakip Pathen in chihna eipeh jouseu mangcha a hilchah le thuhilna kaneiyu hi, amitakip Christa to akiguijopnau chamkimsahna dinga ahi.
English: We proclaim him, admonishing every man and teaching every man in all wisdom, that we may present every man perfect in Christ Jesus;

COL 2:1
Thadou: Keiman nangho le Laodicea a um houbungho chule tahsaa kakimupi loulaiho chengse dinga nasatah a kapohnat peh uhi nahet dingu kalunggot ahi.
English: For I desire to have you know how greatly I struggle for you and for those at Laodicea, and for as many as have not seen my face in the flesh;

COL 3:12
Thadou: Hiche jeh chun Pathen lhenchom mithengte deiumtah angailut namthenga lhendoh nahitah jeh uvin–mikhotona lunggel, mihepi, kineosah, nunnemna lungthim, thohhatna in kivonun.
English: Put on therefore, as God’s chosen ones, holy and beloved, a heart of compassion, kindness, lowliness, humility, and perseverance;

1TH 4:10
Thadou: Tahbeh mongin, nanghon Macedonia pumpia tahsanho jouse nangailut nau navetsah sau ahitai. Hitima chun, sopite, amaho chu hatah a nangailut cheh diu kangeh nahiuve.
English: for indeed you do it toward all the brothers who are in all Macedonia. But we exhort you, brothers, that you abound more and more;

2TH 2:8
Thadou: Chujoutah leh Mihem dan neiloupa hung kiphong doh ding, hinla Pakai Yeshua chun akama ahaidoh hua chu amapa atha ding chule ahungna aloupina chun asuhmang ding ahitai.
English: Then the lawless one will be revealed, whom the Lord will kill with the breath of his mouth and destroy by the manifestation of his coming;

1TI 2:14
Thadou: Chuleh Satan in alheplhah chu Adam ahipon, numeinu joh chu ana lheplhah-a chonset hunglut ahi.
English: Adam wasn’t deceived, but the woman, being deceived, has fallen into disobedience;

1TI 3:2
Thadou: Hijehchun Houbung Upa ding chu ja umtah nolnabei hinkho mang hiding ahi. Aji ang'a kitah ding, ama le ama kitimjoumi hiding, chingthei tah a hing hiding, chule minphat na nei hiding ahi. Jindot them chule mihilthem hiding ahi.
English: The overseer therefore must be without reproach, the husband of one wife, temperate, sensible, modest, hospitable, good at teaching;

1TI 3:3
Thadou: Ama chu julopmi ahiloule agilou hilou ding ahi. Ama chu milungneng hiding, mitoh kinahat hilou ding, chule sum ngailu lou mi hiding ahi.
English: not a drinker, not violent, not greedy for money, but gentle, not quarrelsome, not covetous;

1TI 3:4
Thadou: A-insung kipohtupjou mi, achaten ajathei le athua nunsah joumi hiding ahi.
English: one who rules his own house well, having children in subjection with all reverence;

1TI 5:1
Thadou: Upa tehseho chu phoh hih-in, napa tobang'in jana neitah'in jolthon, khangdong pasalho chu napenpi nasopitah tobang'in kihoupin,
English: Don’t rebuke an older man, but exhort him as a father; the younger men as brothers;

1TI 6:17
Thadou: Hiche leiset a haosaho chu akiletsah louna diuleh kisonpi thei hilou asum u chu kisonna a aneilouna diuvin hilchah in. Ingaichat hou ning lhingset'a eipeuva Pathen joh kisonnan neiyuhen.
English: Charge those who are rich in this present age that they not be arrogant, nor have their hope set on the uncertainty of riches, but on the living God, who richly provides us with everything to enjoy;

1TI 6:18
Thadou: Asum u chu thilpha bolna a aman diuvin seipeh in. Thilpha bolna lama ninglhingu henlang alhasamho khotona hinneiyuhen. Chuleh midang koma phaldoh dingin phattin in kigosan umjing'u hen.
English: that they do good, that they be rich in good works, that they be ready to distribute, willing to share;

2TI 1:4
Thadou: I-kikhen a namitlhilon chu kageldoh in, nangma kamukit nom lheh jenge. Chule iumkhom kit tengleh keima kipana a dimset ding kahitai.
English: longing to see you, remembering your tears, that I may be filled with joy;

TIT 1:2
Thadou: Chuche thutah, jou seitheilou Pathen in vannoi bul kiphudoh masanga ana tepsa, chun tonsot hinna aneiyu chu kisonna apeh ahi.
English: in hope of eternal life, which God, who can’t lie, promised before time began;

TIT 1:7
Thadou: Upa khat chu Pathen insunga gouching ahi, hijeh a chu nolna beiya hinkho amanding ahi. Ama chu kichamsah, lungsabai, ju'a loplou hiding, alamlouva sum ngailu mi hilouding ahi.
English: For the overseer must be blameless, as God’s steward, not self-pleasing, not easily angered, not given to wine, not violent, not greedy for dishonest gain;

TIT 2:12
Thadou: Chuleh eiho Pathen ngaisah lou nale chonset nopsahna a kona kiheimang dinga kihilchah ihiuve. Hiche gitlouna leiset a hi lunglima, chondihna a chule Pathen ngaisahna neiya ikhosah dingu ahi,
English: instructing us to the intent that, denying ungodliness and worldly lusts, we would live soberly, righteously, and godly in this present age;

TIT 3:6
Thadou: Aman hongphal tah in Yeshua Christa vang'in ichunguvah Lhagao theng chu abunglhan ahi.
English: whom he poured out on us richly through Jesus Christ our Savior;

TIT 3:8
Thadou: Hichehi tahsan umtaha kisei ahi, chule nangman hiche thuhil hi hatah a nadopsang ding kadeiye chutia chu Pathen tahsan ho chun thilpha bolding agelkhoh nadingun. Hiche thuhil hohi pha a chule mijouse dinga phachomtah ahi.
English: This saying is faithful, and concerning these things I desire that you insist confidently, so that those who have believed God may be careful to maintain good works. These things are good and profitable to men;

HEB 3:12
Thadou: Chuti ahileh sopi deitahte, Pathen hing jinga kona kiheimangna aso louna dingin chingtheiyun, lungthim gitlouna le tahsanlelna neihih un.
English: Beware, brothers, lest perhaps there might be in any one of you an evil heart of unbelief, in falling away from the living God;

HEB 6:7
Thadou: Vana kon go hunglha chun leiset achapnouvin chule loubol mi dingin Pathen phattheina gapha ahin sodoh in ahi.
English: For the land which has drunk the rain that comes often on it and produces a crop suitable for them for whose sake it is also tilled, receives blessing from God;

HEB 7:16
Thadou: Yeshua thempu hina hi tahsalam dol a Levi phunga mihina ngaichatna pachu hitalouvin, suhmangthei hilou hinna thaneina a konjoh hiya ahi.
English: who has been made, not after the law of a fleshly commandment, but after the power of an endless life;

HEB 7:26
Thadou: Ama thempu chungnung ingaichat u ahina chu Ama athenga le nolna bei, chonsetnen behlou hel ahi. Ama chonsehoa kona chom uma ahin, chule van mun a jabolna sangtah mun changa ahi.
English: For such a high priest was fitting for us: holy, guiltless, undefiled, separated from sinners, and made higher than the heavens;

HEB 8:8
Thadou: Hinlah Pathen in miho chu athemmo nau amu ahitah jeh in, hitihin aseiye: “Pakaiyin aseiye, Keiman Israel le Judah mite toh kitepna thah kasemna nikho hunglhung ding ahi.
English: For finding fault with them, he said, “Behold, the days are coming”, says the Lord, “that I will make a new covenant with the house of Israel and with the house of Judah;

HEB 9:4
Thadou: Hiche dan sunga chun Sana maicham kihal namtui aumin chule thinga kisem thingkonglen Kitepna Thingkong chu aninglia sana jenga kitoma ahi. Thingkong sunga chun sana a kisem bel khat aumin, belsunga chun-Manna, Aaron Tenggol hungpah ado um chule Kitepna Songpheng teni jong aume.
English: having a golden altar of incense and the ark of the covenant overlaid on all sides with gold, in which was a golden pot holding the manna, Aaron’s rod that budded, and the tablets of the covenant;

HEB 9:24
Thadou: Ijeh ham itileh mihem khut a kisa muntheng chu, vana atahbehpa gongso ahibouvin, hichea chun Christa agalutpoi. Ama chu vana alut in Pathen angsungah eiho thalhengin agakilah in ahi.
English: For Christ hasn’t entered into holy places made with hands, which are representations of the true, but into heaven itself, now to appear in the presence of God for us;

HEB 12:5
Thadou: Achate hina jal'a Pathen in nahenguva tilkhounaa athusei chu nasuhmilu hitam? Aman hitin ati, “Ka chapa Pakai thununna chu imalouvin gelhihbeh in, Aman nasuhdih tengleh lunglhahnan neihih in.
English: You have forgotten the exhortation which reasons with you as with children, “My son, don’t take lightly the chastening of the Lord, nor faint when you are reproved by him;

JAS 1:9
Thadou: Tahsan cha avaicha hon kisonna ding khat chu aneiyuve, ajeh chu Pathen in amaho ajabol ahitai.
English: Let the brother in humble circumstances glory in his high position;

JAS 1:19
Thadou: Kasopi deitahteho, hiche hi heuvin, nangho thungaina lama gang uvin lang, thuseiyin kino hih un.
English: So, then, my beloved brothers, let every man be swift to hear, slow to speak, and slow to anger;

JAS 1:23
Thadou: Ajeh chu nangman Thu chu nangaiya chule najui louva ahileh, phatvet a namai vea tobang nahi ding ahi.
English: For if anyone is a hearer of the word and not a doer, he is like a man looking at his natural face in a mirror;

JAS 3:7
Thadou: Miho hin ganhing jouse, vacha ho, a-op a kitholho chule ngaho avah ngoi theicheh-e,
English: For every kind of animal, bird, creeping thing, and sea creature is tamed, and has been tamed by mankind;

JAS 5:14
Thadou: Nalah uva ana damlou um'em? Nanghon houbung upa ho ahunguva, nachung uva Pakai mina thao anuuva chule taona aneina dinguva nakou diu ahi.
English: Is any among you sick? Let him call for the elders of the assembly, and let them pray over him, anointing him with oil in the name of the Lord;

1PE 1:24
Thadou: Pathen Thubun asei dung juiyin, “Mihemte hi hampa tobangbep ahi, ahoinau jong loujaova pahcha pah tobangbep ahi. Hampa agopjin chule apah chu amolloiji.
English: For, “All flesh is like grass, and all of man’s glory like the flower in the grass. The grass withers, and its flower falls;

1PE 5:2
Thadou: Pathen in chin dinga nanganseu kelngoi hon chengse chu chingun. Lungcham tah in, lunghimo louhelin bolun-nanghon ipi phatchomna kakimudoh theidem ti hilouvin, Pathen na natoh nom joh jeh uvin bol jouvin.
English: shepherd the flock of God which is among you, exercising the oversight, not under compulsion, but voluntarily; not for dishonest gain, but willingly;

2PE 1:5
Thadou: Hicheho jouse jal hin, Pathen thutep ho channa dingin kihabol un, natahsan nau chu umchanhoi pendoh nan neiyun, chule umchanhoi penna chun hetna,
English: Yes, and for this very cause adding on your part all diligence, in your faith supply moral excellence; and in moral excellence, knowledge;

2PE 1:6
Thadou: chule hetna chun chang kitim themna, chule chang kitim themna chun thohhatna chule thohhatna chun Pathen ngaisahna,
English: and in knowledge, self-control; and in self-control, perseverance; and in perseverance, godliness;

2PE 2:4
Thadou: Ajeh chu Pathen in vantil achonseho jeng jong akhendehlou ahi. Aman amaho chu muthim lhangkhal kiheh gomtong sunga, Damuna chu alelut jenga, thutanna nikho lhin kahsea dinga akhum tup ahi.
English: For if God didn’t spare angels when they sinned, but cast them down to Tartarus, and committed them to pits of darkness to be reserved for judgment;

2PE 2:13
Thadou: Amaho amanthahna dingu chu thilse abolnau jaljeh a atohgao asan dingu ahi. Amahon sunlai nipi noiya ase bolding chu lunga thanopna aneiyuve. Amaho chu lungsetna bei le setbol mi, nalah uva um ahiuve. Amaho mi doha bolna a athau anomun, nanghotoh nakiloikhom nauva an naneh khomnauva alhauve.
English: receiving the wages of unrighteousness; people who count it pleasure to revel in the daytime, spots and defects, reveling in their deceit while they feast with you;

2PE 2:15
Thadou: Amaho lamdih a kona pampet'a ahitauvin, chule Beor chapa Balaam, thilse bola sumlo nompa khonung juiya ahiuve.
English: Forsaking the right way, they went astray, having followed the way of Balaam the son of Beor, who loved the wages of wrongdoing;

2PE 2:18
Thadou: Ajeh chu amaho pannabei, ngolhoi tah a hamhoithouva ahin, athuseiyuva lamvaina a umho lah a kona hung jamdoh ho chu tahsa lam huhna lung ngaichatnaa miho athujouva lheplhah bai chu athunun jou jiu ahi.
English: For, uttering great swelling words of emptiness, they entice in the lusts of the flesh, by licentiousness, those who are indeed escaping from those who live in error;

1JN 1:2
Thadou: Amatah hinna ahi chu keiho henga kiphongdoh ahitai chule keihon Ama chu kamutauve, chule tua hi keihon kahettohsah uva chule Amatah Tonsot Hinna ahi tia kaseiphongu ahi. Ama Pa toh ana umsa chujouva keiho henga hung kiphongdoh'ah ahi.
English: (and the life was revealed, and we have seen, and testify, and declare to you the life, the eternal life, which was with the Father, and was revealed to us);

1JN 3:21
Thadou: Kagol ngaitahte, eimahon kithemmo channa ineilouva ahileh, Pathen komchu lungngam tah a inailut theiyu ahi.
English: Beloved, if our hearts don’t condemn us, we have boldness toward God;

3JN 1:13
Thadou: Keiman seibe ding tampi kaneiye, hinlah keiman hichu lekhathot'ah kahin sei nom poi.
English: I had many things to write to you, but I am unwilling to write to you with ink and pen;

JUD 1:12
Thadou: Hiche mihotoh hin Pakai ngailutna geldohna a an nehkhom nanei tengu leh, amaho hi twinoiya songpi um tobang, nakong'u kesah thei ahiuve. Amaho hi jachatna neilou kelngoi ching amabou kikhohsah ho ahiuve. Amaho hi leiset chung lama hung kitol lea ahiala go a julhalou meibol tobangbep ahiuve. Amaho hi chavang laiya thingphung, nivei thisa, aga sodohlou ajung geiya kibotdoh tobang ahiuve.
English: These are hidden rocky reefs in your love feasts when they feast with you, shepherds who without fear feed themselves; clouds without water, carried along by winds; autumn trees without fruit, twice dead, plucked up by the roots;

REV 1:4
Thadou: Hiche lekhathot hi John a kona Asia gam'a houbung sagi ho henga ding ahi. Auma, aum jingsa chule ahung umnalai ding; Laltouna maiya Lhagao sagi;
English: John, to the seven assemblies that are in Asia: Grace to you and peace from God, who is and who was and who is to come; and from the seven Spirits who are before his throne;

REV 2:27
Thadou: Amaho chun chitin namtin chunga thih tenggola vai ahom ding chule leibel banga amaho chu avohchip ding ahi.
English: He will rule them with a rod of iron, shattering them like clay pots, as I also have received of my Father;

REV 3:17
Thadou: Nangman kahaove, kadeichan kaneiyin, imacha kangaichapoi nati. Ahinla nangma adapen, khoto umtah, vaichatah, mitcho chule sagohkeo nahi chu nakihetpoi.
English: Because you say, ‘I am rich, and have gotten riches, and have need of nothing,’ and don’t know that you are the wretched one, miserable, poor, blind, and naked;

REV 7:5
Thadou: Judah phunga kona mi sang som le ni, Reuben phunga kona sang som le sang ni, Gad phunga kona mi sang som le sang ni;
English: of the tribe of Judah twelve thousand were sealed, of the tribe of Reuben twelve thousand, of the tribe of Gad twelve thousand,

REV 7:6
Thadou: Asher phunga kona mi sang som le sang ni, Naphtali phunga kona mi sang som le sang ni, Manasseh phunga kona mi sang som le sang ni;
English: of the tribe of Asher twelve thousand, of the tribe of Naphtali twelve thousand, of the tribe of Manasseh twelve thousand,

REV 7:7
Thadou: Simeon phunga kona mi sang som le sang ni, Levi phunga kona mi sang som le sang ni, Issachar phunga kona mi sang som le sang ni;
English: of the tribe of Simeon twelve thousand, of the tribe of Levi twelve thousand, of the tribe of Issachar twelve thousand,

REV 7:16
Thadou: Amaho gilkel kit talou dingu chule dangchah kit talouhel dingu ahi; nisasat in jong amaho akahkhah tahlou hel dingu ahi.
English: They will never be hungry or thirsty any more. The sun won’t beat on them, nor any heat;

REV 13:16
Thadou: Ama chun amitin aneo le alen, ahao le avai, chamlhat le soh hijongleh khut jetlam ahilouleh achalpanga melchihna chu kitah dingin asolin ahi.
English: He causes all, the small and the great, the rich and the poor, and the free and the slave, to be given marks on their right hands or on their foreheads;

REV 16:13
Thadou: Chule keiman lhagao gilou thum uphoh ho tobang jeng chu dragon, sahem chule themgao lhem kam'a konin ahung potdoh kamun ahi.
English: I saw coming out of the mouth of the dragon, and out of the mouth of the beast, and out of the mouth of the false prophet, three unclean spirits, something like frogs;

REV 18:12
Thadou: Amanu hin sana, dangka, khisong mantam, twikoh chang, tupatponnem, ponsandup, lungpon, chule ponsanthip, thinga kisem gimnamtwi, saihaa kisem thil ho, thingmantam'a kisem thilho, sum eng, thih, chule songval-a kisem kong le bel hicheng hohi atam'a tam ana choh ahi.
English: merchandise of gold, silver, precious stones, pearls, fine linen, purple, silk, scarlet, all expensive wood, every vessel of ivory, every vessel made of most precious wood, and of brass, and iron, and marble;

REV 19:1
Thadou: Hichengjou chun, vana mipi atam'a tam awgin tobang kisamging chun, “Pakai chu vahchoiyun, Huhhingna le loupina chule thahat-thilbol theina chu IPathen uva ahi.
English: After these things I heard something like a loud voice of a great multitude in heaven, saying, “Hallelujah! Salvation, power, and glory belong to our God;

REV 21:11
Thadou: Hichu Pathen loupina toh ahungvah doh in chule songmantam tobang'in aemsel in jasper songmantam crystal thenin athengselin ahi.
English: having the glory of God. Her light was like a most precious stone, like a jasper stone, clear as crystal;
